{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements","id":1551903,"title":"Running the Free States - 9 - Crossover Elements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-28T21:45:20-07:00","id":1551903,"title":"Running the Free States - 9 - Crossover Elements","content":"At this point I want to address the non-vampire stuff. This includes crossover elements (werewolves, mages, wraiths, changelings), but also things like hunters and the Arcanum. I am not interested in them for the concepts themselves, but how they might be used in a Vampire game with Kindred PCs specifically in LA.<br /> <br /> Now whether I actually <i>use</i> any of it depends on the players. Some players love the inclusion of these elements and others hate them. Some may like them in theory, but complain in practice (implementation matters). Or they like ghost stories, but hate fairies. So certain elements can be used, but not others. When we do our final pre-game prep, I will be having a discussion with my players as to what they like and don\u2019t like.<br /> <br /> However, even if they don\u2019t want any of these elements in game, this doesn\u2019t mean these elements don\u2019t exist. In the World of Darkness, all these things are just as real and present as vampires. It just means that 1) I shouldn\u2019t introduce them as plot elements, and 2) I should let the players/PCs what areas these things are in so they can avoid them. If they as players want to avoid Lupines for example so should their characters. (It's just important that the characters know about them.) The presence of those elements define what things are actually off-limits. I believe having such limits in the forms of danger zones and such are useful in sandbox style play.<br /> <br /> By the time the LABN sourcebook came out in 1994, besides Vampire the World of Darkness game line had also released Werewolf and Mage so that gets covered. Wraith would be released later that year and Changeling not for a year after that, so they are not covered. So we\u2019ll start with the Lupines.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-02-2026, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T21:51:54-07:00","id":1551904,"title":"","content":"LABN actually does a very good job establishing the Lupine presence in Los Angeles in a fairly short amount of word count. We\u2019re not given many details, but I don\u2019t think their needed for a Vampire sourcebook (this would become an error in future sourcebooks - especially in other game lines - where the crossover element took up way too much space and crowded out page count that would have been better developing their own game more).<br /> <br /> We have three basic areas of Lupine activity, four if you count the Black Spiral Dancers. On the western edge of metro LA we have Lupines at Topanga Canyon in the Santa Monica mountains (Black Furies plus some Uktena). They reactivated a caern back in the early thirties. The sourcebook says the caern is \u201cminor\u201d, but one of the last in this part of the country so it is defended fiercely. The Santa Monica Mountains and nearby Malibu are thus off limits to Kindred. Those who keep showing up here eventually get killed.<br /> <br /> The other area is the Angeles National Forest north of LA. A pack of Get of Fenris and Shadow Lords are here. Nearby is also the Glass Walker tribe in Pasadena and Glendale. They control a lot of agribusiness in southern California, and have a strong interest in Caltech and the Jet Propulsion laboratory. Because of their relative proximity to each other, I am including these two groups together despite their differences. The Glasswalkers are supposed to be the most influential group of Garou in the LA area and have been there the longest (at least among non-Uktena) since 1917.<br /> <br /> Third is a \u201chuge pack\u201d of Bone Gnawers and Uktena in downtown and South Central Los Angeles. Some of the Bone Gnawers belong to the Hood camp and help the downtrodden as best they can.<br /> <br /> The fourth group are the Black Spiral Dancers who occupy a level two Wyrm caern in a pit deep underneath Griffith Park.<br /> <br /> I'll talk about these in detail in future posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T22:05:23-07:00","id":1551905,"title":"","content":"The Santa Monica Mountains and Angeles National Forest make easy borders for the Los Angeles Free States. The Kindred know the Lupines are there and usually avoid them. Vampire characters who want to avoid them can do so easily. We know there is an actual caern and sept in the Santa Monica Mountains. <br /> <br /> No caern is mentioned for the Angeles National Forest. However, if there is not a caern there, the Garou there still need to participate in a sept somewhere. It's highly unlikely it is at the Black Fury and Uktena sept simply because those other tribes are not mentioned. So I prefer to create a new caern there that both groups (Glasswalkers and Fenrir/Lords) can be a part of. It's also possible to create two caerns, one for each group, but I want to limit how many caerns are in the LA area because we've already been told the Topanga Canyon caern is &quot;one of the last&quot;.<br /> <br /> The \u201chuge pack\u201d near downtown LA is a possible point of contention. They are located in the heart of the Kindred domain, and as \u201cthe downtrodden\u201d make convenient food for vampires this would seemingly put Kindred in conflict with them. Yet no such mention is ever made. It\u2019s if the Kindred don\u2019t even know about this pack of Lupines deep inside the city. I imagine this \u201chuge pack\u201d is mostly engaged in scouting and espionage, and probably concentrating more on other Wyrm menaces than vampires. So they avoid combat with vampires entirely. Some pack members might even negotiate with specific vampires for information or favors so if an ST wants to include some less hostile encounters with Lupines this would be the place to do it. Of course, should there ever actually be a war with the Lupines for whatever reason (the sourcebook certainly includes multiple reasons why this might happen), this pack likely strikes fast and violently using whatever knowledge they\u2019ve gleamed about local vampires. However, I intend for this pack to be neutral to Kindred unless provoked. If for any reason players want some Lupine crossover for their characters, this is probably the group of Lupines I'd do it with as encounters don't need to be immediately hostile.<br /> <br /> I'm making this a pack under Coyote. Most members are Ragabash and Theurges with few members of other auspices. That'll make them much more likely to have non-hostile encounters that might lead to cool and interesting scenes with PCs. They are either an anruth pack that frequently travels out of area to different caerns, or perhaps have rediscovered a lost rank 1 caern similar to the Smiling Buddha Sept in Dark Alliance: Vancouver.<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral Dancers underneath Griffith Park presents more flexibility for STs. You can easily ignore them. Use them as some sort of local Griffith Park plot - perhaps involving the Setites. Utilize them as \u201cfriendly\u201d Lupines willing to make deals. Or even activate that tribe\u2019s sometimes alliance with the Sabbat in a Sabbat plot. This pit is supposed to be the major spiritual reason why there is so much &quot;corruption&quot; in Los Angeles, so it does have some relevance to me as a reason for Setite activity. The BSDs themselves won't be active against any vampires, and I can't see why any PCs would ever want to delve underground looking for the pit.<br /> <br /> Not relevant to our needs, the sourcebook also names drops various PENTEX subsidiaries in the LA metro area that can easily explain what the Lupines are doing to fight the Wyrm if they aren\u2019t destroying vampires.<br /> <br /> This is decent enough detail for most STs if they want to consider the inclusion of Lupines in the city or at least map out what areas should be off limits. Three low level caerns around LA does seem a lot to me, but it's the only way I can really explain tribal politics. Keeping all the caerns low level does help me justifying low key Lupine activity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T11:01:04-07:00","id":1551950,"title":"","content":"Time for me to talk with some Gailliards and slip the local Ragabash a suitable <i>douceur</i> for the inside track on local night life - back in a while.<br /> <br /> - SHIFTS TO LUPUS, EXITS -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T11:03:21-07:00","id":1551976,"title":"","content":"Mage is the other splat given some word count in LABN, but we\u2019re told a lot less about them than we are about the Lupines. This is probably because Mage was still in its early period of development, and there wasn\u2019t as many obvious hooks between vampires and mages as there are about vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> There is a Verbena coven in Santa Monica Mountains that tries not to aggravate the Lupines there, and there are Hollow Ones and other Orphans in Hollywood. Otherwise the only mentions of Mages are various Technocracy fronts around Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> Needless to say any ST wanting to run a Mage chronicle set in LA probably adds a lot more mages and sorcerers into the city. However, since vampires are mostly ignorant of what mages do, I don\u2019t find that much of a problem. STs can easily ignore mages unless they have a specific idea for a crossover plot. However, as future posts will show, we do have some other canonical Mage references to LA that can fill some holes for an ST who wants to develop more.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t plan on having one unless the PCs specifically request something. However, just in case I have already made the decision to transplant the Hollow Ones chantry in Book of Chantries from Chicago to the Hollywood environs. That is some low hanging fruit with established ties to vampires. I can make some easy adjustments to fit it better in the local setting. They\u2019ll be there for some easy plot just in case the PCs want something, and I can probably build on this element easily in case it increases instead of whets PC interest in mages.<br /> <br /> I suspect there will be zero crossover with the PCs in this regard. If they do encounter any &quot;magicians&quot;, it's much more likely to be a Sorcerer using the rules in World of Darkness: Sorcerer. However, simply due to my anal need to figure out things beforehand just in case they become relevant, I do like knowing the canonical lay of the land simply because while it does mean more work for me, it's certainly less time than me coming up with things myself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T11:15:29-07:00","id":1551977,"title":"","content":"A mention to LA is made in the Book of Chantries. Since the Book of Chantries was published a year before LABN, it upsets me that cross mentions like this are rarely made in so many regional sourcebooks. You only need a sentence or two to include the mention, and it might have increased sales on that other sourcebook.<br /> <br /> The Vali Shallar chantry is in a Horizon Realm based on the Lost City Z (though called City X in the sourcebook) and inspired by the lost continent of Mu, and therefore the chantry itself is well outside the scope of the chronicle. However, the chantry does have a link to LA with an estate there. One of its cabals, the Yultasi (consisting of Akashic Brothers and Dreamspeakers), controls a cult of Sleepers in LA. These have to be controlled by cabal members visiting the chantry\u2019s Los Angeles Estate. This Sleeper cult serve as scouts and informants, and the cabal is particularly interested in the Progenitors (who attacked the chantry in the past). That estate is also visited by a second cabal, the Hands of Hope (which has some other Tradition members than just Dreamspeakers and Akashic Brothers).<br /> <br /> Not many details are given about the \u201cLos Angeles Estate\u201d. It is a large beachfront estate. It can\u2019t be seen from the road and has typical defenses for a wealthy estate like a large walled courtyard, securtity sensors, five guard dogs, and five servants. It is near multiple ley lines hidden below the Pacific Ocean. A Virtual Adept of the Hands of Hope cabal, Alvin Reynolds, spends most of his time at this estate. He also occasionally plays guitar in a band that has played in a number of local LA clubs.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not told where in LA the estate is. Likely it is not in LA proper. We could place it in Malibu if we want more mages there than just the Verbena, but I also think it would fit somewhere in the South Bay, either one of the Beach Cities or the Palos Verdes peninsula. That's where I'll probably place it.<br /> <br /> Normally I would think this is just trivia, but the description also states that the Yultasi are at odds with several powerful anarch vampires in Los Angeles. The only reason this would happen is that they are trying to protect their Sleeper cult. I don\u2019t think the estate itself is in trouble because otherwise the Hands of Hope cabal would be mentioned. The cultists then must be somehow noteworthy enough to have attracted the attention of some powerful anarchs.<br /> <br /> I presume the Sleeper cultists are some sort of pseudo-Carlos Castenada type New Agers that would fit in well with Dreamspeakers maybe combined with yoga and other alternative medicine types that fit with the Akashic Brotherhood. It\u2019s the type of California mysticism that fits well with the local setting. For them to attract anarch attention, it\u2019s likely something occult in nature. Vali Shallar was founded to \u201cpreserve the old teachings.\u201d The Yultasi also have their own secret library in a safehouse on Earth containing much arcane lore. Unless we want to invent a new location, this library must either be at either Shanghai or Los Angeles (the two places where it is mentioned the chantry has estates on Earth). It\u2019s possible one responsibility of their Sleeper cults is to expand and maintain this library, and perhaps this is one reason they came under the eyes of the anarchs. Once vampire intentions became known, the Yultasi stepped in to protect their informants.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is for the anarch vampires to be lackeys of the chantry\u2019s enemies, but that would be a better idea for a Mage chronicle using Valli Shallar rather than a Vampire chronicle based in LA. So I'll be ignoring this option.<br /> <br /> For my purposes, I\u2019ll have an NPC anarch coterie already inclined to occultism so they can have several run ins with the Yultasi and be warned off. This coterie won\u2019t quite know how to proceed because they don\u2019t understand the nature of the threat. They just know they have angered some powerful magi.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not clear how these Kindred are \u201cat odds\u201d with the Yultasi. That\u2019s a very vague term. It doesn\u2019t necessarily mean enemies or rivals, just that they have contradictory interests. I like the idea that being at odds does not necessarily mean <i>physical</i> violence. Perhaps its conflicts within the astral realm, spirit world, competition for occult resources, and other things that allow for more variety of plots. I'd rather have interesting interactions between PCs and NPCs that can carry over into multiple game sessions than an encounter that ends with the PCs trying to kill everyone.<br /> <br /> If the PCs ever become interested in the more occult aspects of the setting, I might have them learn about this group of Sleeper cultists. I\u2019ll just then see what happens based on what the PCs do. It's entirely possible that I won't bring any Mages at all into this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T11:28:48-07:00","id":1551978,"title":"","content":"There is another small reference to LA found elsewhere in the Book of Chantries. While not given a full description of its own, Balador, a Cult of Ecstasy chantry, has an earthly aspect in Los Angeles. The chantry is important because the canon mage Marianna, possibly the greatest Master of the Cult of Ecstasy, oversees it. It makes a lot of sense to me that the Cult of Ecstasy has some representation in the LA area.<br /> <br /> We aren\u2019t told anything more about its aspect in Los Angeles, but we can easily place it somewhere corresponding to a place where people could have intense physical pleasure that could lead to an ecstatic response. Given the nature of the Tradition, I think it best to not be associated with negative aspects of the sex industry or drug use. I would want something more benign. It\u2019s probably some very posh, exclusive resort where all kinds of consensual hanky panky and bacchanialian celebrations occur. I think free love communes were already passe by 1992.<br /> <br /> That means it would probably be close to LA, but not in the urban environments itself. The Cult of Ecstasy would want something more isolated and exclusive. Perhaps something in Orange County, Ventura County, or possible a small island off the coast (Santa Catalina island is the only one of the Channel Islands that has permanent civilian settlement - five are part of a national park, and the other two are used by the US Navy as training grounds). An exclusive private resort at Santa Catalina would work well IMO.<br /> <br /> Hardly a place vampire PCs might come across, but you never know how actions by the PCs may turn out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T04:54:23-07:00","id":1551994,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve done some quick-and-dirty research into the Garou history in California (In WEREWOLF: THE WILD WEST and those WtA sourcebooks immediately available to me) so what follows is fairly sketchy - also, I need to reread your own posts on the LA situation, since other commitments required me to skim them - so here\u2019s what I have so far.<br /> <br /> BUT FIRST, I absolutely wanted to endorse my pet notion for any \u2018Werewolves in LA\u2019 sourcebook to be titled RAGE ACROSS THE VALLEY.<br /> <br /> No, this doesn\u2019t quite make sense based on the actual geography of Garou LA, but the mental image of a high school hallway with some hilariously cliche Valley Girl in pink slamming a fomori into the lockers whilst a dead ringer for Seth Green looks on haunts me (No, she is NOT in Crinos, she\u2019s in Glabro, I am not a hack).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the actual facts:-<br /> <br /> - As noted, California was a hub for the Uktena (Presumably a major hub, given there seems to have been a significant local population), but the Tribe had lost it\u2019s primacy by primacy by the 1830s.<br /> <br /> At that point just about all the Tribes could be found on the Pacific Coast, but the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Iron Riders and Shadow Lords were already associated with San Francisco &amp; LA by this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> - NOTE: The Silver Fangs, Fenrir and Fianna are said to have led the drive from the East Coast to the Pacific (Though there\u2019s some evidence that Silver Fangs also entered the area through Russian North America).<br /> <br /> In any case the Silver Fangs seem to have become more invested in the Pacific Northwest (Although this is mentioned in a brief, plain statement without explanation).<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Furies appear to have arrived in California with the Spanish, presumably via Mexico: they seem to have made common cause with Elder Brother and Younger Brother whilst shunning the larger settlements, though one would be surprised if familial connections to the settlers never bred trouble between Elder Brother and the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> Given the importance of the mission system to early California, one would be surprised if the Order of Our Merciful Mother played no role in the local Fury population.<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: Younger Brother almost certainly entered California from the Pacific Northwest, after Alaska and Canada their particular stronghold in North America (It should also be considered that Uktena in the West were reinforced by refugees from the East and Southeast: this may well apply to California).<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Bone Gnawers wouod likely have entered California as Mountain Men: in fact it\u2019s possible a few relict populations of the tribe linger in the Sierras and show up in LA from time to time (One wonders how they might differ from their hillbilly counterparts back East?).<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Glass Walkers arrived in California as the Iron Riders (Presumably following the Continental Railroad) and it\u2019s therefore easy to image the region as a place where old Iron Riders made the switch to Corporate Wolves: it\u2019s worth noting that San Francisco and Los Angeles are said to be \u201cmeccas for Urban Werewolves\u201d (and that the San Francisco &amp; LA areas were of interest to the Garou even before serious urbanisation began).<br /> <br /> Why this should be the case I\u2019m not certain, but it occurs to me that the long-term oresence of Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers and Shadow Lords in the region (Coupled with the apparent preference for the redwoods region found in other \u2018European\u2019 tribes) has resulted in a strongly progressive character for the Werewolf populations (Especially coupled with the curious absence of a Silver Fang royal house in the area).<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: The fact that many West Coast Silver Fangs have Russian ancestry may help explain their relatively weak position in the area - courtesy of the first and second Red Scares, though the often republican tenor of US Garou presumably doesn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Speaking of the Shadow Lords, there\u2019s no real explanation for their presence in the region, but I wonder if they may have been drawn in by the general absence of Silver Fang houses and the presence of at least one seriously potent vampire: on the other hand it\u2019s been noted that Black Spiral Dancers entered \u2018The West\u2019 with the Spanish Conquistadors, so it\u2019s possible that both the Black Furies and Shadow Lords were following that particular spoor.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also quite possible they were sick of dodging the Sabbat in increasingly-urban Mexico and liked what they saw in California (Especially the general absence of Silver Fangs until the 1800s).<br /> <br /> <br /> - It also bears noting that the Stargazers have a moderately strong association with California: with San Francisco, obviously, but it\u2019s mentioned that there is at least one tradition that Stargazers might have kept in touch with the \u2018Three Brothers\u2019 tribes even before Columbus arrived in the New World, possibly through their relicts in the future Russian Far East (and the Pacific Coast is the obvious place for these tribes to touch bases).<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: I do wonder if Gaian Garou of non-Native extraction might have been pulled towards the region by the Cataclysm which affected the region in the 1600s, a conclusion that shook the Umbra so hard that the physical landscape of San Francisco felt it (Resulting in a major shift that is said to have opened up the Golden Gate itself, though this may be exaggeration).<br /> <br /> One can only wonder if this may have been felt outside the San Francisco Bay region as well? If it were then it\u2019s not hard to imagine interested parties sending packs on the sort of scouting expedition usually followed up by settlement parties.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s all I have so far (Other than the fact that John Blackfeather, a \u2018Wendigo\u2019, has a career in Hollywood films - presumably in a \u2018Danny Trejo before he was famous\u2019 or \u2018Young Russel Means\u2019 sort of capacity - which might mean he occasionally visits Los Angeles).<br /> <br /> Please pardon the rather rough and ready mix of lore &amp; speculation in this hasty post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T12:18:54-07:00","id":1552009,"title":"","content":"Apologies for not having posted this earlier, but I don\u2019t actually own the sourcebook and had to look this up on White Wolf Wiki - a number of very ancient California caerns are mentioned in CROATAN SONG (All associated with Elder Brother).<br /> <br /> They are (or were):-<br /> <br /> - Sept of the Towering Giants (Sierra Nevada)<br /> <br /> - Sept of the Sheltering Spirit (Santa Cruz, Channel island)<br /> <br /> - Sept of the Pointing Stars (Sierra Nevada)<br /> <br /> - Sept of the Proud Warrior (Joshua Tree, Mojave desert)<br /> <br /> <br /> My research indicates that at least two of these - Sheltering Sprit and Proud Warrior - are fairly close to Los Angeles, so their fate may well be an important part of Garou history in the region (It seems highly likely that the Proud Warrior caern could still be in existence, given Joshua Tree is a national park).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, on another note, I\u2019d bet money that the La Brea tar pits are of interest to the Garou and possibly to Wraiths: they were, after all, been accumulating deaths for a very long time indeed, suggesting a deeply spooky Umbral situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T12:26:46-07:00","id":1552010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019ve done some quick-and-dirty research into the Garou history in California (In WEREWOLF: THE WILD WEST and those WtA sourcebooks immediately available to me) so what follows is fairly sketchy</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I don't have any Wyld West sourcebooks so it'll be interesting to see what's interesting to steal from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case the Silver Fangs seem to have become more invested in the Pacific Northwest (Although this is mentioned in a brief, plain statement without explanation).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting and would make the California region materially different from others where the Silver Fangs have more of a presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IGiven the importance of the mission system to early California, one would be surprised if the Order of Our Merciful Mother played no role in the local Fury population.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good idea and would make that tribe not only one of the first to arrive, but integrate well with any local Uktena and Wendigo. It would help explain why the Black Furies and Uktena worked together to reclaim the caern at Topanga Canyon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bone Gnawers wouod likely have entered California as Mountain Men: in fact it\u2019s possible a few relict populations of the tribe linger in the Sierras and show up in LA from time to time (One wonders how they might differ from their hillbilly counterparts back East?).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a neat aspect of the tribe. I also think the Sierra Nevada mountains would be one of the primary strongholds of the Garou. While urban Garou are a thing in the setting, I try to emphasize their presence in the wilderness and kinfolk towns in remote rural areas rather than in the big cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Glass Walkers arrived in California as the Iron Riders (Presumably following the Continental Railroad) and it\u2019s therefore easy to image the region as a place where old Iron Riders made the switch to Corporate Wolves</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make sense that the Glass Walkers would follow the first transcontinental railroad. I think there's some additional mention of Garou in Caerns: Places of Power in the Children of Gaia section. I'll need to revisit that for my notes at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NOTE: The fact that many West Coast Silver Fangs have Russian ancestry may help explain their relatively weak position in the area - courtesy of the first and second Red Scares, though the often republican tenor of US Garou presumably doesn\u2019t help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Scares didn't target people with Russian ancestry. They were directed against people with ties to radical far left groups and Communist front organizations (and in the case of the First Red Scare, against domestic political opponents of Woodrow Wilson, particularly any peace activists protesting American involvement in WWI) regardless of ethnicity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Shadow Lords, there\u2019s no real explanation for their presence in the region, but I wonder if they may have been drawn in by the general absence of Silver Fang houses and the presence of at least one seriously potent vampire: on the other hand it\u2019s been noted that Black Spiral Dancers entered \u2018The West\u2019 with the Spanish Conquistadors, so it\u2019s possible that both the Black Furies and Shadow Lords were following that particular spoor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It often doesn't make sense where the Shadow Lords are because they were designated as the generic internal &quot;bad guy&quot; within the Garou so they showed up wherever the early game designers thought they were needed. Their involvement with Spanish Conquistadors particularly does not make sense given their heavy kinfolk involvement with the Slavic peoples. In my chronicle, I explained this by saying a significant group of Shadow Lords came with the Vandals who first arrived in Spain and then later went on to conquer North Africa from the Romans. Now we have Spanish Shadow Lords so they can follow where the Spanish go.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea that the Shadow Lords in the Angeles National Forest come from these local Spanish heritage Shadow Lords, and not the Slavic heritage Shadow Lords. It's a neat distinction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also bears noting that the Stargazers have a moderately strong association with California: with San Francisco, obviously, but it\u2019s mentioned that there is at least one tradition that Stargazers might have kept in touch with the \u2018Three Brothers\u2019 tribes even before Columbus arrived in the New World, possibly through their relicts in the future Russian Far East (and the Pacific Coast is the obvious place for these tribes to touch bases).</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense given the association between Stargazers and mountains. The Axis Mundi sourcebook does describe that there were &quot;Stargazers&quot; (meaning Garou whose tribal totem was Chimera; called We-Chon or Falling Stars in the sourcebook) in the New World before the Columbian Contact. Chimera created the Dream Raven spirits (Woneyah Konhe) to help them. Some nice little lore there. They are unlikely to ever come up in LA vampire gang, but in terms of figuring out the greater Garou Nation in California, certainly good to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NOTE: I do wonder if Gaian Garou of non-Native extraction might have been pulled towards the region by the Cataclysm which affected the region in the 1600s, a conclusion that shook the Umbra so hard that the physical landscape of San Francisco felt it (Resulting in a major shift that is said to have opened up the Golden Gate itself, though this may be exaggeration).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to reread that section in Caerns: Places of Power to see what it contains. I imagine though that when it happened, there had to be Eurasian Garou already in the New World (or possibly even in the Old World) who sensed it and travelled there to find out what happened. The game has all these ways for Garou to be sent omens and to travel very far very quickly that it doesn't make sense they'd do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1551994#post1551994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s all I have so far (Other than the fact that John Blackfeather, a \u2018Wendigo\u2019, has a career in Hollywood films - presumably in a \u2018Danny Trejo before he was famous\u2019 or \u2018Young Russel Means\u2019 sort of capacity - which might mean he occasionally visits Los Angeles).</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't recall this character and had to search for him on the White Wolf Wiki. So often the writers of sourcebooks forget that Garou Rage involves the Curse, so I'm glad to see that the auspice of John Blackfeather is not given. That means I don't have to contradict canon to make him a Ragabash who never increased his Rage. A Russel Means or Graham Greene type of actor would be appropriate. I imagine most of his films are not filmed in Hollywood, but on location for pseudo-historical epics like Dances with Wolves, arthouse/indie films set on the reservations, and the occasional TV show that takes place in a &quot;rustic&quot; location and filmed in the Pacific Northwest or Canada. Still, he would have contacts in Hollywood and probably visits from time to time. If he discovers Wyrm minions there in the local film industry, he probably provides that info to the local BF/Uktena sept so they can handle it in a way that does not blow his own cover.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T13:07:40-07:00","id":1552011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552009#post1552009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sept of the Sheltering Spirit (Santa Cruz, Channel island)</div> </div> </div> </div>Santa Cruz Island is where the Earth Mother made the Chumash people according to their mythology so it's not surprising there was a Garou caern there. Currently the island is part of the Channel Islands National park, and what isn't owned by the National Park Service is used for scientific and educational purposes. I imagine there are kinfolk involved there, but that the caern is dormant and there's no local sept - at least in my chronicle. There's just too much human activity in a relatively small area for the Garou to make use of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552009#post1552009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sept of the Proud Warrior (Joshua Tree, Mojave desert)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a vague map of Garou protectorates in my head and notes, and the Mojave Desert is one of them. I was wondering whether to place a caern/sept in the Joshua Tree National Park so this settles it. The Park is almost 800,000 acres (over 400k of which is wilderness) so you can easily hide a caern there.<br /> <br /> It's well east of the Inland Empire region so Kindred in LA can stay clear of it. However, the main highway to LA - Interstate 10 - goes just south of there. That's well over a mile worth of driving. Just south of that is the Imperial Valley, a low populated regions known for the Salton Sea and home to a thriving agriculture economy where I put is another Garou protectorate (actually it's the entire Colorado Desert region which includes the Imperial Valley but extends to the Colorado River) and is the major area of Glass Walker influence over the agriculture business in southern California. <br /> <br /> So that stretch of I-10 (which is about 100 km rural/wilderness and another 100 km of relatively small cities in the Coachella Valley) is a good ambush spot for Garou on Kindred travelling through there. It is easy to justify a situation where Garou can identify and take out Kindred who are using I-10 as a route to LA or away from it. Obviously not all Kindred, but enough that the route is considered more dangerous than normal. Since the distance between LA and Phoenix is at the limit of a full tank of gas for most cars, that area is a popular place to pull over and fill up your gasoline tank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552009#post1552009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, on another note, I\u2019d bet money that the La Brea tar pits are of interest to the Garou and possibly to Wraiths: they were, after all, been accumulating deaths for a very long time indeed, suggesting a deeply spooky Umbral situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The La Brea Tar Pits are briefly mentioned as part of the George C Page Museum of La Brea Discoveries section of the Barony of Angels' &quot;Other Locations&quot; section, but it's just a typical tourist mention. Nothing tied into the supernatural of the World of Darkness. Hancock Park (where the tar pit is located) is only 22 acres large. I agree that it is probably an area of interest to Garou and there should be something special in the umbra about it, but actual Lupine activity is probably fairly low. Kindred can probably visit there without incident. As for wraiths, I'll discuss that later in the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T04:03:05-07:00","id":1552028,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the Shadow Lord prominence in Iberia dates back to the Reconquista, but I don't have any books at hand to check for specifics.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could always base John Blackfeather on Sonny Landham.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T04:27:42-07:00","id":1552032,"title":"","content":"Regarding the &quot;huge pack&quot;, I tend to think of that being maybe eight to ten members (no more than a dozen at the most extreme), probably usually scattered into subunits of three to five. Probably a couple of survivors of an older pack(s) who have found themselves mentoring a low Rank misfit collection of teen runaways, gutterpunks, and people trying to avoid gang life.<br /> <br /> And if you want an offbeat totem for such a pack, you can always have them follow the spirit of the colony of feral chickens that have lived under the Vineland Ave. offramp of the Hollywood freeway since the early 1970s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T12:28:29-07:00","id":1552039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552032#post1552032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the &quot;huge pack&quot;, I tend to think of that being maybe eight to ten members (no more than a dozen at the most extreme)</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicle notes, I put the membership of this pack at ten. That is certainly a lot larger than most packs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552032#post1552032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">probably usually scattered into subunits of three to five. Probably a couple of survivors of an older pack(s) who have found themselves mentoring a low Rank misfit collection of teen runaways, gutterpunks, and people trying to avoid gang life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including teen runaways and other lost kids is a good call out to the early days of Werewolf when it is was heavily implied the teen runaway phenomenon was caused, in part, to the First Change and Lost Cubs. Local Bone Gnawers (and Uktena) finding such lost souls and providing them a &quot;home&quot; is a great idea. (Maybe that is even the pack's real &quot;purpose&quot;). This pack could be a bunch of misfits surrounding a core of experienced veterans who can mentor and look out for them. They can group the kids into smaller subunits to help bond them together, gain common experience, and send them out on missions appropriate to their skill level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552032#post1552032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you want an offbeat totem for such a pack, you can always have them follow the spirit of the colony of feral chickens that have lived under the Vineland Ave. offramp of the Hollywood freeway since the early 1970s.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollywood_Freeway_chickens\" target=\"_blank\">I did not know that!</a> That is an interesting piece of local lore. I've now recorded that in my notes. It's always handy to have interesting local lore like that. It makes the chronicle seem more &quot;real&quot; to me when the ST can include real trivia like that.<br /> <br /> However, I'm going to go with Coyote as the pack totem. Since coyotes are now everywhere in LA, I think it's appropriate for a pack there to be under it. I also wanted a pack totem that whose guidance and theme would not lead to the pack actively attacking vampires. So Coyote's loose ethics, trickster ways, and so on would be a good way to emulate that. (Also the freeway chickens are all the way in the San Fernando Valley, not near downtown LA where the huge pack is supposed to be. Would still be a good place for them to visit sometimes!) I'm putting their rank 1 caern in the basement of a seedy bar near <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skid_Row,_Los_Angeles\" target=\"_blank\">Skid Row</a>. It's a cross between the Smiling Buddha caern in Dark Alliance: Vancouver and <a href=\"https://fightclub.fandom.com/wiki/Lou%27s_Tavern\" target=\"_blank\">Lou's Taven in Fight Club</a> where Tyler Durden starts hosting the weekly matches. Except the basement doesn't hold fight clubs, but the sept's activities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BqWwPIU55ec\" data-code=\"BqWwPIU55ec\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BqWwPIU55ec/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm actually stealing a lot from Fight Club because there is a template in the Revised Brujah Clanbook which is clearly based on Ed Norton's character from the movie, and I thought Project Mayhem (and the real world groups it is based on) would make a great coterie/gang of anarchs. Alas, the Coyote pack gets Lou's Tavern though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T14:32:03-07:00","id":1552043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552028#post1552028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Shadow Lord prominence in Iberia dates back to the Reconquista, but I don't have any books at hand to check for specifics.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could always base John Blackfeather on Sonny Landham.</div> </div> </div> </div> R.E. The Shadow Lords in Iberia, I would assume their presence in Spain at exactly the right time to hop a galleon to the New World might well be connected to the debut of House Wyrmfoe on the world stage - given the House was connected with the Netherlands, France and Spain in those days, it\u2019s highly likely that they would become bound up with the House of Burgundy and then the Habsburgs who succeeded to the dignities of Burgundy and the brand-new Spanish monarchy in the person of the Emperor Charles.<br /> <br /> Given the latter\u2019s ties to Central Europe, the Shadow Lord\u2019s well-attested love of being \u2018The Man Behind the Man\u2019 and their pathological desire to keep Silver Fang royalty under careful observation, it\u2019s not hard to imagine a number of Grandfather Thunder\u2019s very own rocking up in Spain as it became a Great Power, presumably doing well enough to become established in the fighting tail of House Wyrmfoe and then getting sent to the New World to do the Silver Fang\u2019s more thankless chores, as per usual.<br /> <br /> Given the flight of a significant number of vampires to the Americas, it\u2019s even possible that Shadow Lords were brought in to deploy their expertise on the Leeches to determine what the heck was going on, tailing them to the New World and then getting the bright idea to reassure the bosses back home that there was nothing to see here, no problem, minor vampire problem, please send word to Uncle Martin to bring Cousin Isabella and the kids.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, the Shadow Lords took one look at two whole near-mint condition continents with no Silver Fangs and decided to corner the local rackets before the boss back home showed up to make some noise, with the end result that not a few 16th/17th century Shadow Lords abruptly became \u2018Spanish\u2019 Shadow Lords under mysterious circumstances.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile House Wyrmfoe gradually became English and/or British enough to sail for New England, rather than New Spain, resulting in their eventually becoming the first All-American Royal House of the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T14:40:52-07:00","id":1552044,"title":"","content":"Also, one look at Santa Carla island made me think \u201cThat is home away from home for the Black Furies\u201d even before you mentioned that it was legendarily associated with a Great Mother goddess \u2026 you know, there might be some seriously dark comedy in the tale of how a place so perfectly suited to the Furies remains spiritually-dead to them, despite what I suspect to be more than one century of interest on their part.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Sept of the Proud Warrior, it\u2019s<br /> impossible not to imagine this as the place where one tribe\u2019s sacrifice was offered up to the Rite of Still Skies - given it\u2019s fabulous antiquity and the very name, it\u2019s almost <i>too</i> perfectly suited for the role (Heck, it might well have played a role in binding the Storm Eater for the very first time too).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll bet cash money that the Uktena have a powerful interest in the place, no matter their situation in the rest of California: for some reason one imagines Rattlesnake as the patron of this particular caern (Not least because his ability to share ancestral memories not of their own lineage with his children compliments the sheer age of the site perfectly \u2026 and it doesn\u2019t hurt that his Ban requires followers not to wage war on the Pure Ones).<br /> <br /> Not sure whether this should be a Caern of Wisdom or Honour though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T14:49:38-07:00","id":1552045,"title":"","content":"If you have never seen it, you might get some mileage out of Penelope Spheeris's 1984 film Suburbia, about a group of teen runaways squatting in an abandoned LA neighborhood (complete with packs of feral dogs). It is sort of a fictional companion piece to her earlier documentary The Decline of Western Civilization, about LA's early 80s punk scene. (Also TDoWC's two sequels about the late 80s metal scene and the 90s gutterpunk subculture.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T16:37:38-07:00","id":1552047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552045#post1552045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have never seen it, you might get some mileage out of Penelope Spheeris's 1984 film Suburbia, about a group of teen runaways squatting in an abandoned LA neighborhood (complete with packs of feral dogs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I've seen that movie although at the time it was under one of its alternate titles. I can't remember which one. One of my players actually introduced it to me back in the day. My favorite part is when someone accidentally calls the character &quot;Razzle&quot; by the actor's name (Flea from the Red Hot Chili Peppers) and he responds, &quot;My name is Razzle, man!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a terrible movie in many regards (not a surprise given its very limited indie budget), but it gives a great snapshot of young street kid punks in LA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T16:57:50-07:00","id":1552172,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also going to mention some sorcerers here. To me, using mages or sorcerers doesn\u2019t really matter to the setting or the PCs in a Vampire game. They serve the same narrative focus. Personally, using the original WoD: Sorcerer sourcebook is actually a lot easier for me than Mage.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m mostly leaving what sorcerers will be present as pretty open. I can plug more in as needed. However, in terms of NPCs planned in advance, I will be putting a member (perhaps two in case the main one needs an assistant) of the Nephite Priesthood here.<br /> <br /> Why? Because there are actually a lot of Mormons in southern California (I think about 80,000 in LA metro although it\u2019s over 700k in California as a whole in the early nineties). Mormon involvement in California is quite old, and there\u2019s been a Los Angeles Branch since 1895. There\u2019s also significant Spanish speaking Mormons in LA because of Mormon missionary activities in Latin America and immigration to the US. Having a member of the Nephite Priesthood can provide a little extra kick to Mormon vampire hunters just like the Society of Leopold does for Catholic vampire hunters. Why shouldn't they have their own Van Helsing? They might never show up in the chronicle, but I like to think ahead in terms of potential hunters. They'll only come into play if one of the PCs for whatever reason targets someone in the Mormon population. The Los Angeles Mormon temple is located in the Westwood neighborhood which I believe is in Louis Fortier's barony. I don't know any of the local demographics, but I assume it's fairly spread out with some local clumping like with most religious denominations.<br /> <br /> There is also the Thal\u2019hun based out of San Francisco. I have an odd liking of them because they show that Paths of Sorcery don't need to be &quot;magic&quot; per se. They are just collection of mechanical effects that can utilize a lot of different flavor text. Their fringe pseudo-science of vibrational resonances creating effects (their Paths) isn\u2019t quite what people expect from \u201cmagic\u201d, but it might be something explored by occult, pseudo-scientific, or perhaps even musical oriented characters. Easy enough to have a small group of Thal\u2019hun in LA itself. Very unlikely any vampire PC will come across this group, but sandbox elements like this can present STs options based on PC actions. Most likely, it\u2019ll just be some Easter egg type stuff hidden under normal California weirdness. Any PCs who run into them will need a very compelling background that adequately provides a good reason why they might encounter them.<br /> <br /> If I'll introduce anyone other than this, it'll probably a group from the Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites because of the all Thelemite activity that's been done in LA since at least the twenties. Any other occult groups will probably just be fronts for other supernatural groups.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T02:40:39-07:00","id":1552189,"title":"","content":"\u2018Mormon Van Helsing\u2019 is one of those wonderful, slightly hilarious sentences that makes exploring the World of Darkness such a fascinating experience - heck, even more amusing than horrifying.<br /> <br /> On a good day, right up until nightfall.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m getting a mental image of Mormon Van Helsing as surprisingly-young, painfully earnest and weirdly prone to sing to himself as a coping mechanism (In the same way Abraham Van Helsing occasionally bursts out laughing at the absurdities of horror, just so that he doesn\u2019t have to start screaming).<br /> <br /> Bonus points if he\u2019s visibly a ginger, in an homage to the literary Van Helsing, and visibly freckled for that \u201cOh God, I\u2019m too young for this ****\u201d energy appropriate to a Mormon missionary.<br /> <br /> At this point I\u2019m severely tempted to make him more of a Jonathan Harker (or perhaps a Mina Harker*) than a Van Helsing.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Novel, not \u201cPfft, Vampires are hot, Mina was TOTALLY into it\u201d World of Darkness version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T12:19:31-07:00","id":1552211,"title":"","content":"There's a distinction between Mormon vampire hunters (who could be anyone) and the &quot;sorcerers&quot; of the Nephite Priesthood. That group of sorcerers is based on a &quot;secret&quot; book of Nephi that Joseph Smith did not include in the Book of Mormon because it was not meant for public knowledge. Instead, the now celestial being Nephi revealed himself to the Mormon Uriah Spence in 1849 and restored the lost &quot;Nephite Priesthood&quot; who can unleash certain Paths of Sorcery as miracles they can call upon God through prayer. Although I don't think it is stated so in WoD; Sorcerer, I believe any such Nephite Priests must be male because the Church of Latter Day Saints does not ordain female priests. (Other STs, of course, can do whatever they want.)<br /> <br /> The Nephite Priests mostly wander the Mormon Corridor, but can go anywhere where they feel they are needed. California is outside the Corridor, but has a significant population in numbers so some Nephite Priests probably frequently visit there. So if a PC vampire happens to prey on the local Mormon population, I would not have one show up at first. He should be the equivalent of summoning up the heavy supernatural artillery when everything else doesn't work (like Father Merrin in The Exorcist). There's no reason why one of the priesthood can't have more experience in killing vampires than others, the equivalent of someone like Sullivan Dane or Caiaphas Smith.<br /> <br /> I have long thought the Nephite Priesthood is one of the more interesting groups in WoD: Sorcerer, and they're an element you can really only use in certain locales. Although I doubt this will actually come up in play, I like having it in my back pocket for LA. Depending on how things go, maybe I'll even make some future member of someone's Herd or other background, or a rival to someone's Influence be a Mormon just to see if it can build up to something where this guy appears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T14:37:05-07:00","id":1552215,"title":"","content":"I sometimes wonder if any of the older Thal'hun members were involved with Jack Parsons and his occult groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T17:06:05-07:00","id":1552218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552215#post1552215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes wonder if any of the older Thal'hun members were involved with Jack Parsons and his occult groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per WoD: Sorcerer, the Thal'hun post-date Jack Parsons quite a bit (he died in 1952), and their brand of fringe pseudo-science does not match Parson's Thelemite style occultism.<br /> <br /> As written, the Jeva prophet Khuvon incarnated in 1961, taught his disciples for five years before being &quot;freed from his mortal shell&quot;, and afterwards his seven disciples formed the Star Council of Zoraster to carry on his work. &quot;Jeva&quot; were the 300 members of the extraterrestrial race Hui:xa who phased into a different space-time continuum and became beings of pure energy so they could teach other planets enlightenment and the science of thal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JvDAHmQ1_tw\" data-code=\"JvDAHmQ1_tw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JvDAHmQ1_tw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Reading between the lines, someone had a psychotic break in 1961, called himself Khuvon, proclaimed a space alien philosophy to some friends, and died in 1966.<br /> <br /> Thal'hun seems like Scientology by way of Richard Shaver combined with UFO religions like Raelism. It fits well with the California New Age movement from the sixties and seventies.<br /> <br /> There's probably an actual new religious movement associated with it, and only a small handful of people who could be counted as &quot;sorcerers&quot; themselves. WoD: Sorcerer says there are 55 (as of 1997) people in the Thal'hun society itself. I would say those 55 are people in various stages of actually to master &quot;thal&quot; (not all actual &quot;sorcerers&quot;, those who can actually &quot;set a resonance&quot; are probably quite small, maybe 1-2 dozen. However, it would make sense their beliefs are held by a few hundred or thousand people worldwide (they have a newsletter!). Their headquarters is in a mansion in San Francisco, not far from Golden Gate Park.<br /> <br /> As crackpot &quot;religions&quot; / pseudo-science go, it's not a bad one to use in the LA Free States. However, there is probably even less of a chance the PCs will run into them than they will the Mormon Van Helsing. I'll probably name drop them though as just another weird California thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T20:08:07-07:00","id":1552222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552218#post1552218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Per WoD: Sorcerer, the Thal'hun post-date Jack Parsons quite a bit (he died in 1952), and their brand of fringe pseudo-science does not match Parson's Thelemite style occultism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in the sense of some of the younger people who hung around Parsons (or L. Ron) right after WW2 drifting through Southern California's various New Age occult and alternative religion scenes over the following decades before finding the Thal'hun. Some sort of Silent Generation beatnik turned sex cultist turned LSD psychonaut turned Khuvon disciple. If nothing else, it would make an interesting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T10:59:39-07:00","id":1552235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552222#post1552222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant in the sense of some of the younger people who hung around Parsons (or L. Ron) right after WW2 drifting through Southern California's various New Age occult and alternative religion scenes over the following decades before finding the Thal'hun. Some sort of Silent Generation beatnik turned sex cultist turned LSD psychonaut turned Khuvon disciple. If nothing else, it would make an interesting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I misunderstood. Thanks for clarifying. It's certainly possible some minor associate or hangers on, who were more occult dilettantes than serious Thelemites, could fall into Thal'hun later on. However, I think the original seven disciples who later formed the Star Council were likely not one of them. I associate them with being much younger, more impressionable, and more New Age thinkers that best fit the California of the mid sixties and later rather than. But that is just a personal preference, and other STs can handle things differently. (Although strangely if someone wanted to investigate &quot;Khuvon&quot; himself, I'd be open to considering whether there might be someone like that who is awfully similar to Khuvon. Who (or what) Khuvon is, is left totally open.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T11:19:26-07:00","id":1552237,"title":"","content":"The Arcanum sourcebook mentions that the San Francisco chapterhouse was opened back in 1910. Even if a chapterhouse is located in San Francisco instead of LA, that is still close enough for the ST to run any Arcanum centered plots and have any Arcanum scholars in LA be heavily supported by that organization. (And it might provide a reason for PCs to visit SF and thus the Vampire Club.)<br /> <br /> One of my great personal frustrations with the Vampire setting is that while the Arcanum always seemed liked it would be an important part of Vampire chronicles, that never seemed to occur. The close relationship between certain members of the Talamasca and vampires in Anne Rice novels never translated to the World of Darkness. Perhaps the more lax approach to the Masquerade in LA will provide more opportunities for an Arcanum scholar or investigator to attach to the PCs?<br /> <br /> There just happens to be a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated\">current thread on the Arcanum</a> in the general World of Darkness forum and using them in a chronicle so I'll link that here. General comments on the Arcanum can easily go there, but if people have specific comments on the San Francisco chapterhouse or using them in an LA Free State chronicle, they'd be welcome here.<br /> <br /> I want to have at least one Arcanum scholar (and perhaps multiple mortal informants/investigators utilized by the Arcanum who aren't aware of the reasons/purpose they are paid) in Los Angeles. I haven't decided how integrated/knowledgeable that scholar is with the Kindred of LA. However, I've been wanting to include the Arcanum heavily in a Vampire chronicle for a long time, and it is probably now or never. Maybe give that scholar a slight edge like some form of psychic numina like Clairvoyance, Precognition, or Psychometry. Something that could justify the scholar being able to make contact with one of the PCs. Not any highly developed Psychic Power, just enough to provide an edge and justify contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T17:37:22-07:00","id":1552247,"title":"","content":"There was an obscure two-season show from the 1970s called The Sixth Sense, about a professor of parapsychology at UCLA who had ESP abilities and did occult investigations. I always thought that would make for a really interesting LA based Arcanum member, especially in the 70s or the 90s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T19:41:25-07:00","id":1552249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552247#post1552247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was an obscure two-season show from the 1970s called The Sixth Sense, about a professor of parapsychology at UCLA who had ESP abilities and did occult investigations. I always thought that would make for a really interesting LA based Arcanum member, especially in the 70s or the 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first I have heard of that show. I couldn't find any episodes on YouTube just some brief bits, a promo, and the title sequence.<br /> <br /> Given that the Arcanum researches many different kinds of occult activity, it's certainly likely there are multiple Arcanum investigators in the LA area, each researching a different topic. If for any reason a PC should also become involved or investigate one of these other topics, it could provide another, easier way to introduce the Arcanum to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T00:04:32-07:00","id":1552255,"title":"","content":"I forget, did LA by Night say anything about local mummies? I recall it coming out at that point when the 1st ed Mummy was almost forgotten and 2nd ed didn't exist yet, so I suspect they might have been overlooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T03:26:31-07:00","id":1552259,"title":"","content":"When it comes to local mummies you probably need to ask the local daddies, baby.\ud83e\udeae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T10:20:41-07:00","id":1552263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552255#post1552255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, did LA by Night say anything about local mummies? I recall it coming out at that point when the 1st ed Mummy was almost forgotten and 2nd ed didn't exist yet, so I suspect they might have been overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question. <br /> <br /> I don't recall any mention of mummies in the LABN sourcebook. I also don't recall any mention of Los Angeles in either the 1e or 2e Mummy sourcebook although I believe they did mention both Chicago and New York. (I don't own the Revised era version of Mummy, and I think it does a terrible job of emulating the traditional (cinematic) horror mummy. So for my own chronicles, I only use the earlier sourcebooks.)<br /> <br /> Given the importance of Los Angeles to the Followers of Set, I imagine the city has to be watched by at least one mummy loyal to Horus. And the many amenities the city has might have attracted at least another mummy not as active in Horus' war with the vampires. Because I believe there are not many actual mummies in existence (and also because I believe if you want to keep things special, don't overdo them), I'm loathe to have multiple mummies in any one city. However, given the size and importance of Los Angeles as a global city, I do think having more than one mummy can be justified. I wouldn't have more than three though. And in terms of any mummy actually meeting the vampire PCs, I'll only be keeping it to one unless there's some really unexpected roleplay happening.<br /> <br /> Unlike many crossover elements, I feel Mummy can fit very well with Vampire. It's not as potentially disruptive as other elements, and the two share a lot of the same gothic themes. I'll need to give some thought to a few mummy character concepts that would fit well. I'm less concerned about the mechanical/power aspects of the characters because I don't intend them to be antagonists to the PCs or Kindred in general. Possibly a potential ally against the Setites. So any powers displayed would be more for purposes of appropriate flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T10:48:31-07:00","id":1552264,"title":"","content":"There is a Twilight Zone episode, Queen of the Nile, which has an immortal Cleopatra passing herself off as a series of glamourous Hollywood actresses, and I always thought that would be a cool idea for a WoD mummy in LA. Someone who was some form of entertainer back in the Bronze Age and has just kept at it over the millennia in different forms, settling in LA at the dawn of Hollywood and still at it in their new public persona. The idea would work with either gender, and they may secretly run their own talent agency or production company, giving them more opportunities for vampire entanglements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T11:08:50-07:00","id":1552265,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> God help the Nosferatu if this Mummy gets wind of their name for annoyingly-pretty priority targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, it\u2019s perfectly possible for there to be only one <i>resident</i> Mummy in LA whilst the city is important enough for there to be a number of semi-regular visitors (Especially if said visitors are old friends paying a call on the resident).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T11:46:37-07:00","id":1552270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552264#post1552264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Twilight Zone episode, Queen of the Nile, which has an immortal Cleopatra passing herself off as a series of glamourous Hollywood actresses, and I always thought that would be a cool idea for a WoD mummy in LA. Someone who was some form of entertainer back in the Bronze Age and has just kept at it over the millennia in different forms, settling in LA at the dawn of Hollywood and still at it in their new public persona. The idea would work with either gender, and they may secretly run their own talent agency or production company, giving them more opportunities for vampire entanglements.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I went with that, I would want to go with a more behind-the-scenes angle to avoid the issues of celebrity. Maybe a musician - but not a pop music star. Instead someone who worked in an orchestra role who could play concerts and events with a group, be a session musician, help on movie soundtracks, and the like. Still be involved in (multiple) entertainment fields and keep an eye on Setitie/vampire activity, but not be noticeable. In case her eternal youth or identity changes ever gets spotted, she could masquerade as a high humanity vampire (I remember that as a template in Mummy 2e) or perhaps a ghoul. Without a Prince to approve progeny and a poor system of tracking who is coming or going, there's much less chance of their backstory unravelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552259#post1552259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it\u2019s perfectly possible for there to be only one <i>resident</i> Mummy in LA whilst the city is important enough for there to be a number of semi-regular visitors (Especially if said visitors are old friends paying a call on the resident).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. I was thinking of having a second mummy be located in the general southern California vicinity, but not necessarily in LA itself. Maybe a winery owner in Santa Barbara county or a linguistics expert at Monterey for the Defense Language Institute. They're both out of the way, but within easy commute to multiple centers of vampire influence or just to enjoy the amenities of those cities in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T12:00:18-07:00","id":1552291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552010#post1552010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's some additional mention of Garou in Caerns: Places of Power in the Children of Gaia section. I'll need to revisit that for my notes at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I finally rechecked Caerns: Places of Power to see what else it contained in the CoG section besides the Sept of the Western in Muir Woods National Monument north of SF.<br /> <br /> It mentions there are Bone Gnawers in Golden Gate Park who have a low level caern hidden in the city. There's nothing wrong with that, but my instincts are to reduce the number of caerns when I can to reflect their supposed scarcity. I think some Bone Gnawers in SF are fine, but there's no reason why they can't utilize the caern at Muir Woods when needed. After reading the terrible way they run the Sept of the Green in New York, I don't think they're exactly the best caern protectors anyway.<br /> <br /> There are also Glass Walkers in Silicon Valley involved in finance and technology. Presumably these are the Walkers that the Ventrue vampire Stephan Workman sometimes works with.<br /> <br /> There's also a Stargazer and his Wendigo student <i>somewhere</i> in the area. The Stargazer is named Morihei High Mountain. Morihei is a Japanese given name and likely best known as the given name of the founder of the martial art airkido, Ueshiba Morihei (which I am pretty sure is the reason for his name). Normally I would place this kind of character far from any city since the Stargazers like isolation and there are lots of nearby mountains. However, it says he is in contact with and helping a Nosferatu who is searching for Golconda.<br /> <br /> I haven't explored Golconda much yet in designing the chronicle. There's no reason why there can't be such a Nosferatu somewhere in the Bay Area. Simply because I'm lazy, I just may move Alexander Danov (from Gary, Indiana mentioned in the first corebooks in the Forged in Steel chronicle) out here. He's supposedly well known for in North America for his search for Golconda. So perhaps he never quite made it to Chicago in my chronicle, or he decided to move on from there. He'd be an interesting guest at the Vampire Club and be another strong Nosferatu NPC to interact with for the Nosferatu PC.<br /> <br /> There is a BSD pack living in the SF sewers (which must complicate things for any SF Nosferatu wishing to utilize it), but they are actually arrivals who were previously at the Horrid Hole Pit in Death Valley. (This means there are two pretty bad sources of evil in Death Valley, this BSD hive and the Great Temple of Set mentioned in Clanbook: Setite). Presumably the two have some kind of association as early sourcebooks often tie the Setites and BSDs as allies of a sort. <br /> <br /> The text says that Charles Manson mentioned it in his ravings, which is likely due to the Manson Family's use of the Barker Ranch at Death Valley as their &quot;headquarters&quot; in 1968/1969. Given its prominence in local California legend, I wonder if I should fictionalize the Manson Family and their murders so I can utilize them in some capacity in the chronicle. I often use roman-a-clef versions of real people in order to not be exploitative or in bad taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T08:38:24-07:00","id":1552369,"title":"","content":"I may have mentioned this before, but it amuses me to imagine John Blackfeather - \u2018Hollywood Wendigo\u2019 - as the student of this particular Stargazer sage (If only because it would highlight his nature as a very progressive son of Younger Brother and also give him another reason to be close enough to Los Angeles to dip in for the occasional adventure or misadventure).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Regarding the quest for Golconda, it makes perfect sense that a vampire pursuing this goal would be more a pilgrim than a hermit (and it\u2019s inherently more interesting for the character to have left a city and a situation with which the Players are likely to be broadly familiar, since this highlights his desire to break the shackles of his immortal condition).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m not saying you HAVE to to make one of the more loyal followers of \u2018Not Charles Manson, we just went to the same finishing school\u2019 a lady called \u2018Marilyn\u2019 but the rather dark in-joke is certainly there to be made.<br /> <br /> <br /> - On a more serious note, I wonder if the Setites were drawn to Death Valley by the local hive or vice versa? (Here\u2019s a question: are these two locuses of villainy the source of the local Evils or were they drawn here by some corrupting influence older than themselves?).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T12:56:38-07:00","id":1552386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552369#post1552369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the quest for Golconda, it makes perfect sense that a vampire pursuing this goal would be more a pilgrim than a hermit (and it\u2019s inherently more interesting for the character to have left a city and a situation with which the Players are likely to be broadly familiar, since this highlights his desire to break the shackles of his immortal condition).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an aspect I had not considered. Not only could he be a resource pointing towards Golconda, but he also might be a way for a PC to learn some lore of what happened in their old city. I told the PCs that they'd be arriving in LA fresh off the boat and to pick one domain east of the Mississippi River to come from. While I don't think anyone choose Chicago, Danov could easily have spent some amount of recent time elsewhere as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552369#post1552369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, I wonder if the Setites were drawn to Death Valley by the local hive or vice versa? (Here\u2019s a question: are these two locuses of villainy the source of the local Evils or were they drawn here by some corrupting influence older than themselves?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there is some lost evil calling out to them. There is obviously a Pit there so there is a concentration of supernatural evil. Whether the BSDs or Setites got there first depends on the ST. Previously there could have been (or still is!) some Uktena Banetenders guarding the place.<br /> <br /> The Shoshone people have <a href=\"https://www.legendsofamerica.com/ca-queendeathvalley/\" target=\"_blank\">legends</a> on why Death Valley is the way it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T04:58:17-07:00","id":1552449,"title":"","content":"Well that legend of the First Nations has WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE written all over it - in fact if you look at it from the right angle one could even infer the corruption of a Caern, as recalled by those on the outside looking in (I\u2019ve tended to assume that the \u2018Pure Ones\u2019 were closer to their Kin than many tribes, but never entirely transparent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T11:54:00-07:00","id":1552456,"title":"","content":"I am also considering possible inclusion of the demon cult, Cult of the Black Heart, mentioned in the first Book of Madness. The Black Heart cult is supposed to be world's largest demon cult with over 12,000 members worldwide and includes a few vampires as well. Individual covens are lead by a diabolist high priest with actual infernal investments and dark sorcery. They do classic Black Mass style rituals with classic Satanism type stuff. Its arch-priest that rules the cult was a former acolyte of the Celestial Chorus which I take is meaning is actually a defrocked Catholic priest, which is supposed to be a requirement to perform a Black Mass in classic folklore. The cult worships one of the Archdukes of Hell, Grostolis (though I imagine most cultists just call him Satan or the Devil).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7tlrHtaVLEw\" data-code=\"7tlrHtaVLEw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7tlrHtaVLEw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm very tempted at including this simply because the motif of aspiring celebrities selling their soul to Satan is classic Hollywood. I am a bit concerned that including this plus the Setites (as well as other occult groups I have planned) is a case of too many things covering the same ground. However, Infernalism and Typhonism is not the same thing, and I think as long as keep the Black Heart as an organization clearly separate from vampires, it won't be overlap. It'll provide a nice distraction from vampires in general. Like a lot of planned sandbox elements, running into them really depends what the PCs do. If one runs with the celebrity/LA glamor crowd, there's a good chance of encountering one of the covens in LA.<br /> <br /> I could easily make any Hollywood Satanism group it's own thing, but I figured tying it into an existing (but obscure) canon group just makes it a nice Easter Egg for the setting and alleviates some amount of work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T17:48:14-07:00","id":1552470,"title":"","content":"I was intending to move onto Wraith next, but instead I'll be talking about hunters in the chronicle because of the recent discussion concerning some <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1552459#post1552459\">characters mentioned in the original Hunter's Head in another thread</a>. It is very debatable whether hunters are considered &quot;crossover&quot;, but I did not think there would be substantial enough discussion about them on their own and this was the next best spot for them.<br /> <br /> Hunters generally did not get much discussion in Vampire setting sourcebooks despite the corebook's Forged in Steel setting utilizing multiple hunter characters with strong ties to the NPCs. That generally holds true in LABN with one exception which is very original, but he's somewhat buried in the text. That would be Reverend Leon Cutler who is at the center of a vampire hunting group inside the Bloods criminal gang (or as the sourcebook names its fictional counterpart, the Blood). We're given very little information about Leon Cutler or the other members of the Blood who hunt the vampires of the Crypt's Sons.<br /> <br /> Cutler and his followers seem to target the Crypt's Sons exclusively, likely because the Crypts have exclusive feeding domain over much of the African-American neighborhoods in Los Angeles, and Cutler is defending his own people being preyed on by vampires (who all happen to be from the Crypts). As a result, the other vampires in LA seem to realize that there are vampire hunters among the Blood, but don't do anything about it because they fear the numbers and power of the Crypt's Sons. In fact, Salvador Garcia secretly helps Leon Cutler by donating to his church and providing him information, all through intermediaries. That's about all we get. Even though the introductory adventure at the end of the sourcebook is directly tied to the Crypts-Blood gang feud, the only additional information we get is that Cutler is an older black man and his church is a gleaming white church that takes up half a block in the middle of the Watts neighborhood (the church and Reverend Cutler himself does have True Faith).<br /> <br /> It's an intriguing premise that needs more detail. While I may have overlooked it, I don't even think we get the religious denomination of Reverend Cutler. Is he Baptist, Methodist, Pentecostal, or something else? So we'll need to figure that out, add a group of key Blood leaders who are also aware of the vampires, and decide on the lower gang members who do the actual hunting. Considering the Blood seems to battling the Crypts to a standstill despite the presence of two dozen or so vampires, this has to be a fairly potent organization. It also present a rare opportunity for most PCs in a hunter plot, a group of hunters who probably won't go after them and could be interacted with.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of potential here provided the hard work is put into it to flesh it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T12:15:33-07:00","id":1552505,"title":"","content":"The original Hunters Hunted sourcebook has several characters that can easily be used in a Free State chronicle. I'll start with one of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> mentioned: Deborah Rose Keller. Keller was a suburban housewife of a physician when her son was kidnapped and murdered in an occult ceremony. In response she became a public advocate and began researching similar occult style murders and crimes across the country. She became known as a &quot;rituals crime&quot; expert and become frequently consulted by police departments across the USA. She's like a combination of John Walsh and Tipper Gore.<br /> <br /> Keller found enough evidence that she became convinced there was kind of occult conspiracy behind these crimes, and this being the World of Darkness, this could actually be true. Once she realized her theories about certain evidence was making police think she was a nut, she clammed up, toned down her public statements, and continued her investigations in private. At some point she encountered a real vampire and managed to escape alive, now knowing vampires are real. At the time of Hunters Hunted, she had not yet uncovered another vampire, but she's still well known enough that her name is recognized by many Kindred and Princes. She's also made some kind of connection with the Society of Leopold and presumably therefore has seen other evidence of vampire activity.<br /> <br /> Keller herself has some decent attributes on her character sheet. High Social and Mental skills, and three dots in Empathy, Leadership, Investigation, and Occult. She also has the Backgrounds of Allies, Contacts, and Resources, but I think that understates her influence. It's more of an indication of what she can bring directly to bear. She's fairly famous around the country and has a &quot;huge following among other concerned housewives and citizen's groups.&quot; As a recognized expert on &quot;ritual crimes&quot;, she also has some limited respect among law enforcement. She often tours the country giving seminars to police, citizens groups, and PTAs. Her ties to the Free States specifically is that it is mentioned she lives in California, and therefore I'm arbitrarily assigning her to Orange County specifically.<br /> <br /> By herself, she's not much of a threat. It's really her role as a public advocate against &quot;occult murders&quot; that can create problems for the Kindred and PCs. What she really needs is some kind of public group like the Parents Music Resource Center (the infamous committee created by four wives of prominent Washington DC politicos, including Tipper Gore that helped create the &quot;Parental Advisory&quot; warning label on music albums) and the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children. Like those, it should have some other members and have some big funders. It needs to act as an information clearinghouse and resource for parents, children, law enforcement agencies, schools, and communities to assist them in solving occult crimes and raise public awareness about ways to prevent those kinds of crimes. I imagine a not inconsiderable number of people involved have lost loved ones to vampires in some way - either as victims killed when feeding or &quot;cult involvement&quot; that lead to them disappearing as they became members of Herds or became ghouls or similar. Not to mention crimes committed by other supernaturals like infernalists, nephandi, Black Spiral Dancers, and other creatures.<br /> <br /> I envision most hunters in general likely target the vampires of the Sabbat instead of the Camarilla or independent clans. The Sabbat is just a lot more sloppy and leaves a lot more evidence. This group would not be different, plus the Sabbat's various ritae more closely resembles the kind of occult ritual crimes this group investigates. It's not that Camarilla Kindred do not engage in such activities, it's just that they are involved in things like the Sabbat Creation Rite, the Blood Bath, the Blood Feats, the Festival of the Dead, and the Palla Grande which involved a lot of ritual aspects and mortal deaths. I imagine these activities provide the basis for a lot of occult crime sites that are proof of a &quot;occult conspiracy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus I'm sure Keller is documenting who among these local law enforcement seem to be real allies (police who have independently come to the conclusion of an &quot;occult conspiracy&quot; or vampires) and who may be secret enemies (which may number any number of clueless police or just those who don't want to be seen as crazy, but also has to be a significant number of police under vampire influence/domination/blood bond).<br /> <br /> I would probably never have Keller herself become involved in any plot. Instead, it would be local citizens groups, perhaps families of the victims or vampires, who use or assist Keller's organization. Keller herself simply runs the organization at a high level, builds networks, and is often on mass media. Make her and the group be seen as something potentially dangerous to the Kindred and lessen the idea that vampires control everything and don't have anyone pushing back against them. It's also a good group to use for any family members of the victims of the PCs to join or help fund. A parent whose daughter who mysteriously disappeared and whose body was later found drained of blood would be a good choice. Also, given the idea that such a group more likely than not exposes or identifies activities of the Sabbat more than the Camarilla, it could be a good way for other vampires to use in their struggle against the Sabbat. We can also utilize Keller - or more likely someone trained by her or her group in proper investigation techniques of occult crimes - to serve as a good outside consultant helping law enforcement. And possibly knowing a great deal about certain Sabbat rites, blood magic rituals, etc. in a lot more detail (but in a clinical way) than someone &quot;should&quot;. In general, I think it's a good &quot;low level&quot; hunter threat in the sense that it can heighten concern for PCs to hear their name mentioned, but it isn't a threat that can be immediately solved with violence.<br /> <br /> The anarchs of the Free States, of course, are somewhere in the middle. They lack the obvious depravity and ritual of the Sabbat, but don't have the discipline or internal policing of the Camarilla. Many LA anarchs won't be exposed, but some of the more outrageous anarchs and their activities may be identified. Since I'm placing Keller somewhere in Orange County, I'll also base her organization in one of the cities there.<br /> <br /> We really a good name for this group. Names can really make or break concepts like this. Maybe something like the National( or American) Center/ (or Alliance, Foundation or similar) Against Occult Crimes. If people have any suggestions for the name of this group, I'd love to hear them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T15:59:06-07:00","id":1552508,"title":"","content":"I have over the years fiddled with the idea of a group I refer to as &quot;Cultbusters&quot; - this is very much a placeholder name, as it lacks the sort of gravitas for something akin to the PMRC, MADD, or even DARE (and as you mentioned, really needs to be an acronym for that full 80s effect) - who are essentially what you describe: Concerned parents and family members of &quot;cult victims&quot; augmented by a smattering of sympathetic law enforcement, media, and professional deprogrammers as well as the occasional opportunistic politician.<br /> <br /> I have mainly focused on this as a thing for Werewolf and, to a lesser degree, Changeling, but it has a lot of carry over into Vampire as well. Especially in regard to Blood Dolls and blood cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T17:10:11-07:00","id":1552509,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Rev. Cutler should be played by Keith David.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T11:37:37-07:00","id":1552515,"title":"","content":"There's another group of hunters mentioned in the Hunters Hunted that have direct relevance to the LA Free States. This is a motorcycle &quot;gang&quot; known as the Young Bloods. They're essentially a group of independent ghouls who now hunt vampires to get their vitae. They were just a group of young criminal hoodlums from LA. The book calls them &quot;motorcycle enthusiasts&quot; who would get into trouble so they were not actual criminals, but I'm sure they qualified for violating traffic laws, public disorder, some vandalism and that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> Anyway their wacky hijinks attracted the attention of the Brujah vampire Lamar who made them ghouls. It was great fun for a while until they got tired of Lamar lording it over them, so they staked and destroyed him. Fearing that Lamar's vampire friends would go after them, they fled. However, they craved the rush of vitae in their system so they've begun to hunt vampires. They renamed themselves the Young Bloods because of course they would. In 1992 they really only just started, but they've already become known to the Kindred.<br /> <br /> There are fifteen of them, four of which are women. The only name we know is their leader Bob and another guy named Rod. They are &quot;becoming known to many Princes,&quot; one of who has declared a Blood Hunt on them. They are said to roam the highways and streets of America, but they seem to concentrate on the West Coast as there are rumors they are actually pawns of the Camarilla killing many off anarchs on the west coast. Their members have to have the five point flaw Hunted by Kindred. That is pretty much all we are told.<br /> <br /> I wondered if this group was ever updated and checked out Ghouls: Fatal Addiction. While that sourcebook does mention a group called the Young Bloods (which seems to originally come from Midnight Circus), they are clearly not the same group. The name just gets used again.<br /> <br /> That's a decent start on an unusual group of hunters with a non-typical motivation with strong ties to the LA area. However, there are a lot of details to figure out. <br /> <br /> First, what do they do for money? They need money for gas, maintenance and repair of their motorcycles, food and lodging as they travel, and so on. Even outlaw biker hooligans need to earn a living. What the hell are they doing? Petty criminal acts can only get them too far. Real criminal enterprises would create too many problems from more established criminal bikers and law enforcement. Doing odd jobs only gets them so far and leaves a paper trail. The best I can come up with is that when they destroyed Lamar they found a big, but portable source of cash that has let them get by, and they supplement that as best they can whenever they destroy another vampire. It's not the best of plans as they'll eventually run out of ready cash, but I guess that can be part of their storyline.<br /> <br /> Second, where exactly is their scope of activities? While we're initially given what appears to be them going all over the USA (presumably so an ST can use them wherever their chronicle is located), other details hint that it is mostly the west coast and their victims are mostly anarchs. I'm going to keep them mainly out west, mostly utilizing I-5 and the Pacific Coast Highway with some regular visits to Arizona, Nevada, and New Mexico. They do make occasional forays to the Midwest, South, and East Coast. It's enough that they've become &quot;known&quot; to many Princes, but they're mostly scene as a problem for the anarchs and left alone. For the one prince who has declared a blood hunt, it's either because the Young Bloods destroyed someone the prince really cared about or that they've become a local political issue. That implies it is probably one of the princes close to the Free States. Maybe Prince Vannevar of SF?<br /> <br /> Third, while these are mostly goons, there has to be something special about them to account for their success. Even in their origin story, it is not typical for a group of ghouls to turn on their domitor and destroy him so quickly afterwards just because they got tired of his lordly ways. Is Bob unbondable? Could even more members be unbondable? They don't know much about vampire society, but nevertheless they are good at detecting lone vampires and picking them off. This just can't be due to luck. Do they just have good instincts? Does one or more of them have some strange Merit that makes them good at detection? Or perhaps a psychic power like aura reading? Are they being secretly assisted by someone? There's probably a lot of stupid young vampires among the anarchs who will leave too much evidence, but that can't happen all the time. And for those who do, how much evidence would be available to a group like this?<br /> <br /> Fourth, assuming they've had a lot of success around the Anarch Free States, you need to identify characters in advance who have lost friends to them, particular any coterie mates of Lamar. In fact, maybe all of Lamar's friends are now destroyed, having gone after the Young Bloods at some point (perhaps individually), but underestimated them. Once the other anarchs put things together, they realized there was a dangerous group out there and put out word at the rants.<br /> <br /> Fifth, while their mobility is the most important asset, I don't imagine they spend all their time on the road or that they only utilize cheap motels. Do they have regular places they crash - abandoned cabins, friends' houses, vacation homes or park trailers unused for most of the year by their owners? Give some thought to their logistics. That'll provide bread crumbs for any PCs pursuing them.<br /> <br /> Although most of the fifteen members should be seen as essentially disposable by the ST and don't need much development, there does need to be some thought given by the ST. When the PCs run into them, the ST needs to know enough to portray them as more than ciphers. If the PCs decide to wipe out the Young Bloods, they may want to observe them for a while before deciding on a plan. Any one single member of the Young Bloods would be easy to defeat, but fifteen makes them a menace. They have enough members too that any action against them won't likely eliminate all of them. This means the group will likely show up again and can be used repeatedly, building on each previous encounter/story. So it is best if the surviving members have some real personality and flair so that they are memorable and make interesting repeating antagonists.<br /> <br /> Since the Young Bloods are very opportunistic hunters, they are not going to stick around long. They should move on quickly after each kill or attempted hit. Whether they're successful or have failed, it's smart of them to just leave. Still plenty of evidence for PCs to investigate somewhat, but the next encounter will come when the ST desires, not them. They are not going to target any one specific vampire or stick around to defend a beloved mortal victim. They just want to drain the vampire and move on to their next hit. They should also target lone vampires, avoiding groups of multiple vampires. Their only real advantage is numbers so it's best for them to preserve that. As such, it's likely they'll never target the PCs themselves. Instead, the PCs might make it their mission to stop them.<br /> <br /> A group like the Young Bloods is inherently disposable. They're young and stupid so if they die, it's not a big loss to the ST like losing a competent cell of the Society of Leopold would be. But they are large enough you can keep using them for multiple game sessions and hopefully build some personal stakes, memorable encounters, and interesting antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T11:55:23-07:00","id":1552518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552509#post1552509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Rev. Cutler should be played by Keith David.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d bet cash money THEY LIVE was a formative influence on the original sourcebook\u2019s version of the Good Reverend and his cohorts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T11:59:11-07:00","id":1552519,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I would like to point out that if you\u2019re going to throw Vampire Hunters into World of Darkness LA, it would be a crime not to remind yourself that BAYWATCH\u2019s Mitch Buchannon literally moonlighted as an occult investigator (When not being a Boss Lifeguard, charmingly goofy single dad and a Special Forces veteran whose former CO was played by an ex-James Bond) and take this as inspiration for at least one LA BY NIGHT character.<br /> <br /> Especially if your players are getting a little too bored or a little too cocky and can use some hearty Nineties cheese in their diet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T13:33:10-07:00","id":1552521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552505#post1552505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Hunters Hunted sourcebook has several characters that can easily be used in a Free State chronicle. I'll start with one of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> mentioned: Deborah Rose Keller. Keller was a suburban housewife of a physician when her son was kidnapped and murdered in an occult ceremony. In response she became a public advocate and began researching similar occult style murders and crimes across the country. She became known as a &quot;rituals crime&quot; expert and become frequently consulted by police departments across the USA. She's like a combination of John Walsh and Tipper Gore.<br /> <br /> Keller found enough evidence that she became convinced there was kind of occult conspiracy behind these crimes, and this being the World of Darkness, this could actually be true. Once she realized her theories about certain evidence was making police think she was a nut, she clammed up, toned down her public statements, and continued her investigations in private. At some point she encountered a real vampire and managed to escape alive, now knowing vampires are real. At the time of Hunters Hunted, she had not yet uncovered another vampire, but she's still well known enough that her name is recognized by many Kindred and Princes. She's also made some kind of connection with the Society of Leopold and presumably therefore has seen other evidence of vampire activity.<br /> <br /> Keller herself has some decent attributes on her character sheet. High Social and Mental skills, and three dots in Empathy, Leadership, Investigation, and Occult. She also has the Backgrounds of Allies, Contacts, and Resources, but I think that understates her influence. It's more of an indication of what she can bring directly to bear. She's fairly famous around the country and has a &quot;huge following among other concerned housewives and citizen's groups.&quot; As a recognized expert on &quot;ritual crimes&quot;, she also has some limited respect among law enforcement. She often tours the country giving seminars to police, citizens groups, and PTAs. Her ties to the Free States specifically is that it is mentioned she lives in California, and therefore I'm arbitrarily assigning her to Orange County specifically.<br /> <br /> By herself, she's not much of a threat. It's really her role as a public advocate against &quot;occult murders&quot; that can create problems for the Kindred and PCs. What she really needs is some kind of public group like the Parents Music Resource Center (the infamous committee created by four wives of prominent Washington DC politicos, including Tipper Gore that helped create the &quot;Parental Advisory&quot; warning label on music albums) and the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children. Like those, it should have some other members and have some big funders. It needs to act as an information clearinghouse and resource for parents, children, law enforcement agencies, schools, and communities to assist them in solving occult crimes and raise public awareness about ways to prevent those kinds of crimes. I imagine a not inconsiderable number of people involved have lost loved ones to vampires in some way - either as victims killed when feeding or &quot;cult involvement&quot; that lead to them disappearing as they became members of Herds or became ghouls or similar. Not to mention crimes committed by other supernaturals like infernalists, nephandi, Black Spiral Dancers, and other creatures.<br /> <br /> I envision most hunters in general likely target the vampires of the Sabbat instead of the Camarilla or independent clans. The Sabbat is just a lot more sloppy and leaves a lot more evidence. This group would not be different, plus the Sabbat's various ritae more closely resembles the kind of occult ritual crimes this group investigates. It's not that Camarilla Kindred do not engage in such activities, it's just that they are involved in things like the Sabbat Creation Rite, the Blood Bath, the Blood Feats, the Festival of the Dead, and the Palla Grande which involved a lot of ritual aspects and mortal deaths. I imagine these activities provide the basis for a lot of occult crime sites that are proof of a &quot;occult conspiracy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus I'm sure Keller is documenting who among these local law enforcement seem to be real allies (police who have independently come to the conclusion of an &quot;occult conspiracy&quot; or vampires) and who may be secret enemies (which may number any number of clueless police or just those who don't want to be seen as crazy, but also has to be a significant number of police under vampire influence/domination/blood bond).<br /> <br /> I would probably never have Keller herself become involved in any plot. Instead, it would be local citizens groups, perhaps families of the victims or vampires, who use or assist Keller's organization. Keller herself simply runs the organization at a high level, builds networks, and is often on mass media. Make her and the group be seen as something potentially dangerous to the Kindred and lessen the idea that vampires control everything and don't have anyone pushing back against them. It's also a good group to use for any family members of the victims of the PCs to join or help fund. A parent whose daughter who mysteriously disappeared and whose body was later found drained of blood would be a good choice. Also, given the idea that such a group more likely than not exposes or identifies activities of the Sabbat more than the Camarilla, it could be a good way for other vampires to use in their struggle against the Sabbat. We can also utilize Keller - or more likely someone trained by her or her group in proper investigation techniques of occult crimes - to serve as a good outside consultant helping law enforcement. And possibly knowing a great deal about certain Sabbat rites, blood magic rituals, etc. in a lot more detail (but in a clinical way) than someone &quot;should&quot;. In general, I think it's a good &quot;low level&quot; hunter threat in the sense that it can heighten concern for PCs to hear their name mentioned, but it isn't a threat that can be immediately solved with violence.<br /> <br /> The anarchs of the Free States, of course, are somewhere in the middle. They lack the obvious depravity and ritual of the Sabbat, but don't have the discipline or internal policing of the Camarilla. Many LA anarchs won't be exposed, but some of the more outrageous anarchs and their activities may be identified. Since I'm placing Keller somewhere in Orange County, I'll also base her organization in one of the cities there.<br /> <br /> We really a good name for this group. Names can really make or break concepts like this. Maybe something like the National( or American) Center/ (or Alliance, Foundation or similar) Against Occult Crimes. If people have any suggestions for the name of this group, I'd love to hear them!</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m not going to lie, seeing a group with Big Peter Cushing Energy is delightful. As for possible names for this organisation, please allow me to suggest -<br /> <br /> - American Parents Against Ritual Abuse (APARA)<br /> <br /> - American Families Against Unconventional Crime (AFAUC)<br /> <br /> - American Families Against Cult Abuse (AFACU)<br /> <br /> - American Families Against the Abuse of the First Amendment (AFAAFA)<br /> <br /> - American Parents in Defence of the First Amendment (APDFA)<br /> <br /> <br /> Note: one assumes that the more legally minded/Liberal members of this organisation would place great emphasis on the organisation being simultaneously committed to Freedom of Relgion and to ensuring that First Amendment rights are not abused by Occult ********.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Committee for the Defence of the First Amendment (CDFA)<br /> <br /> - Free Exercise Defence Organisation (FEDO), named for the \u2018Free Exercise\u2019 clause of the First Amendment.<br /> <br /> - Free Exercise Observance and Defence Organisation (FEODO)<br /> <br /> - Council for Defence of the First Amendment (CDFA), or perhaps \u2018Citizens\u2019?<br /> <br /> <br /> - Citizens Against Ritual Abuse (CARA): this might be an especially compelling name if the acronym commemorates a loved one who was lost to the night.<br /> <br /> - Citizens for Responsible Exercise of the First Amendment (CREFA).<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point the names seem to be getting a tad repetitious, so I\u2019ll give it a rest and a little more thought. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T13:33:57-07:00","id":1552522,"title":"","content":"It strikes me that an organisation with the initials \u2018CARE\u2019 would be perfect, but I can\u2019t think of a suitable abbreviation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T18:47:30-07:00","id":1552523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552521#post1552521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not going to lie, seeing a group with Big Peter Cushing Energy is delightful.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Deborah Rose Keller is not Lawrence Van Helsing, she probably has someone like him as an occult expert/scholar who can provide an academic explanation on occult rituals or conspiracies. A Montague Summers or Sabine Baring Gould for the modern day. Their key contribution being a secular, forensic, non-supernatural evaluation of occult rituals and crimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8U9i00dOJYM\" data-code=\"8U9i00dOJYM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/8U9i00dOJYM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Plus someone who can explain how dangerous Black Dog Game Factory's roleplaying games are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nFIWUYr0n10\" data-code=\"nFIWUYr0n10\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nFIWUYr0n10/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The emphasis of Keller's organization isn't the supernatural (though she now knows it exists), but crime, especially murder and probably sexual abuse as well. It's just that many of the perpetrators aren't mortal humans involved in the occult, but actual supernatural creatures themselves. So the organization isn't there to convince families of the victim that their tragedy had a supernatural cause, but help parents prevent occult crimes against their family and assist the police in finding the perpetrators.<br /> <br /> So for Keller to actually hunt vampires herself (even indirectly), she really needs to find someone like CPD Detective Gregory Stephens or FBI Special Agent William Shepherd from the original corebooks. I imagine as an organization, Keller will be slowly identifying people who also know/believe vampires are real and recruit them. It'll be sometime before it can become a true hunter organization herself. The fact that someone in the Society of St Leopold made contact with her is suggestive that the Society sees Keller and her group as useful to their hunts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552521#post1552521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for possible names for this organisation, please allow me to suggest -</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some nice names. APARA is probably my favorite of them.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking of some variant of Occult Crimes Research Center, Occult Crimes Prevention, or Occult Research Center. Some form of &quot;occult&quot; or &quot;ritual&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is there any way to do a voting poll on this forum?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-19T19:07:33-07:00","id":1552533,"title":"","content":"Parents Against Cult Activity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T12:30:16-07:00","id":1552547,"title":"","content":"The other hunter mentioned in Hunters Hunted that might show up in LA is Dennis Quincy, the Uncanny Danny. He's a stage magician/paranormal skeptic in the vein of James &quot;The Amazing&quot; Randi. He has vast media support and is a prolific author. Randi himself was a somewhat frequent guest on The Tonight Show with Johnny Carson and appeared on a variety of other TV shows. If Dennis is our analogue, he can likely show up in LA at any time convenient to the ST regardless of where he actually lives. He's only had one vampire encounter, but it was sufficient to make him realize that they do, in fact, exist.<br /> <br /> How to use him though?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> mentioned a possible small group of hunters who were illusionists/mentalists. The only problem with that is such a group is likely to be skeptics so the only reason they would ever join such a group is if they had incontrovertible proof of vampire existence. It would be very hard for Dennis to recruit any fellow skeptics in that community. They just won't believe him, and Dennis can't exactly reproduce what happened to him. He knows he'll sound like a nut. So unless the ST just claims these other mentalists had similar experiences, it'll be hard to have a group like that IMO.<br /> <br /> Of course Dennis could use his scientific and investigation skills to find other surviving victims, but they'll be of any number of beliefs about vampires. They won't necessarily share Dennis' own materialist philosophy.<br /> <br /> Because despite Dennis encountering a vampire, I don't think it means Dennis thinks the supernatural is real. We're told that after the attack he came up with a scientific theory to explain vampirism. He won't look for a paranormal explanation. I think it is much more likely he'll attempt to explain them in terms of a &quot;scientific&quot; paradigm. Eventually that attempt might collapse under the weight of cumulative evidence that simply can't be explained by science, but that may take a long time. I think it's far more likely his initial theories might be some consideration that it is a result of some kind of parasite, parallel evolution, or something else. Maybe some combination of the vampires from The Strain, Necroscope, or Whitley Streiber's Keepers. It could go increasingly fringe science for a long time as he learns more, but he'll likely reject outright magical or supernatural explanations.<br /> <br /> The one interesting thing about a &quot;hunt&quot; from Dennis is that it's basically done as a result of scientific curiosity and the advancement of knowledge. It won't primarily be about protecting people (though I think that would also be important in the long run). So a hunt won't be about destroying a vampire to protect or avenge one's loved one. It'll be about capturing a specimen for analysis, autopsy, investigation. That may mean Dennis' first evidence might be captured ghouls or thin bloods rather than actual full blooded Kindred simply because they're less powerful and easier to capture intact or kill and examine their corpse.<br /> <br /> However, before he can do that, he'll still need to recruit people to help him, as well as think through the possible legal ramifications of his experiments. Kidnapping, corpse stealing, possible &quot;murder&quot;, or unauthorized autopsy/dissection are crimes that could see him prosecuted. He would want to avoid that. That may also mean his first entry into a chronicle might not be as an &quot;active&quot; hunter, but someone who shows up at the morgue, crime scene, or other secured location that has evidence he wants to see, and gains access to it (and perhaps steals it).<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of the character, but I do think it will take a lot of work to introduce him into a chronicle. I see this as a lot of steps slowly building up the idea that someone may be secretly investigating scenes of obvious Masquerade breaches (hopefully by NPCs, not the PCs) and some time before the PCs figure out it is this famous skeptic/magician.<br /> <br /> I would sorely love to have a small team around him, perhaps the equivalent of Allies and Contacts rather than teammates or retainers (his character sheet in HH shows Contacts 4, Fame 2, Resources 4, and Reputation 1). Dennis is very much an intellectual challenge, not a physical one. Although not listed on his character sheet, I'd consider giving him a Merit like Iron Will or Unbondable, or simply making him one of the &quot;Neutrals&quot; often mentioned in early Vampire sourcebook lore as those who are simply immune to Dominate.<br /> <br /> It's also worth mentioning that Dennis' one encounter with a vampire was someone who clearly intended to embrace him. She states she intended to give him a &quot;gift&quot; which he can enjoy throughout &quot;eternity&quot;. So it is possible this vampire is still out there, stalking him, and she might be very protective of him and hostile to anyone who intends him harm. Nothing is said about this vampire other than she had one ghoul (whose job was to lure Dennis to his regnant), that she was beautiful (but that may be more a result of Presence rather than Appearance), and that she has glowing red eyes (indicating Protean 1). My gut instincts assigns this vampire to the Malkavian clan, but she could easily be most clans without a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T13:57:48-07:00","id":1552550,"title":"","content":"I always felt like Dennis would have been an interesting member of Null Mysterius from Hunter: The Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T11:00:33-07:00","id":1552564,"title":"","content":"Another possible source for hunters is the FBI Special Affairs Division, first detailed in Hunters Hunted, but expanded in Project: Twilight. The first two corebooks mentioned an FBI agent in their Gary, IN chronicle adventure, but he was simply a lone FBI agent who had become convinced of supernatural activities. <br /> <br /> HH shows a rather small SAD with only five field agents, three lab techs, a director (George Thomasson) and another admin (called a second in command), all presumably based in DC.<br /> <br /> Project Twilight shows a much bigger SAD lead by Gerald Osbourne, but keeps it in continuity by saying Kindred manipulations got Thomasson fired, but that SAD expanded greatly due to the &quot;Grubbholb Case&quot; in 1993 when a US Senator made sure SAD was highly funded after his granddaughter disappeared after a pack of wolves ransacked the family's country estate. This would expand SAD's interest into werewolves (Project: Twilight was a WtA sourcebook after all). In this version, SAD is a far larger division with many agents, much more resources, and regional directors (including one Thomas Little as the West Coast Director, presumably based in LA). For any sourcebook detailing government hunters, you pretty much need to have a larger organization to justify the sourcebook.<br /> <br /> I think how an ST proceeds really depends on personal tastes and the chronicle needs. Do you want a much larger SAD style organization (or even a Second Inquisition style one)? Or do you prefer the much smaller Mulder/Scully and X-Files approach of HH (although this precedes the X-Files)? Or even just keep it to local FBI agents (and other local law enforcement officials) like William Shepard and Detective Gregory Stephens in Chicago?<br /> <br /> I'll probably keep it as small as possible. Despite my recent hunter posts here, I don't find hunter plots to actually work well in game. They tend to lead to dead ends, and players rarely act imaginatively. I would either need to destroy PCs during the day, or have hunters act stupid and attempt to fight them at night. I don't like either of those. The first angers players. The second makes me upset. So I now typically limit hunters as a background element that targets dumb NPCs in the hopes this scares (or reminds) the PCs to act smart. Their presence is a good justification to force other NPCs to take actions on the Masquerade. Only if I think the appearance of hunters will add something interesting to the game would I even try introducing them into actual play and interaction with the NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T12:29:26-07:00","id":1552593,"title":"","content":"Any discussion of hunters will likely inevitably bring up the Society of St Leopold, so here we are. In the LABN sourcebook itself, I don't believe there is any mention of the Society. Nor do I think southern California is mentioned in the Inquisition sourcebook, so we're entirely on our own. I am normally hesitant to establish any significant presence of the Society. They should be rare. Any established cenaculum likely has some powerful members and resources (at least compared to ordinary hunters). They should only be found in predominantly Catholic areas, and likely are founded only when there is significant evidence of vampire activity, which in my chronicles tend to be in areas not controlled by the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> However, southern California seems to qualify in all of those categories. Between a quarter and a third of southern California's population is nominally Catholic. The anarchs are much sloppier at the Masquerade than the Camarilla is, and roving Sabbat packs are common. A major cenaculum here could support Society activity not only in southern California, but the Southwest in general, including Mexico.<br /> <br /> The Inquisition sourcebook only has a brief high level description of the Society in the United States. There are five provinces dividing up the entire country (Mid-Atlantic, Southeast, Northeast, Midwest, and West). The text actually mentions &quot;six&quot; provinces, but then gives us only five regions although it states the Western province may soon split into two. This is probably just bad editing. We're told the oldest US cenacula are in Philadelphia, Baltimore, New Orleans, and Boston. The only provincial cenacula we're told is in the Brookland neighborhood of DC, so that is clearly in charge of the Mid-Atlantic Province, not withstanding the age of Philadelphia and Baltimore cenacula. Boston is most likely the home to the Northeast provincial, and New Orleans the Southeast provincial. The Midwest and West Provinces must cover a huge territory, but we're not given any hint of where their provincial cenaculum is located. For our purposes here, it's also important to note that the entirety of Mexico and Central America is one province, and that its provincial is located in Mexico City, home of the oldest cenaculum in the Western Hemisphere. They must be consumed with fighting the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Because of the way Prince Maria of San Diego was destroyed (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550753#post1550753\">mentioned, surprisingly, in a post on the Sabbat thread</a>), I have arbitrarily decided San Diego is the best location for a major cenaculum. My idea is basically that inquisitors destroyed Maria back in 1945, and that cell stayed to establish a cenaculum there. Since Tara provides a more &quot;princely&quot; leadership to her anarchs in the city, her coterie doesn't tend to be bothered by it. Other anarchs she tolerates in the city sometimes run afoul. It's mainly Sabbat who get gacked since they tend to leave a lot more evidence and are very active in next door Tijuana. Although technically part of the Central American province, I imagine most activities in Tijuana and surrounding territory is actually done by the inquisitors here with reports also going to Mexico City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T12:32:03-07:00","id":1552594,"title":"","content":"<br /> There is also a cenaculum in Los Angeles simply given its sheer size, but it is basically just a safehouse with real support coming from San Diego instead. The Society is active there, but because Reverend Cutler is a more &quot;important&quot; hunter figure in LA, I don't want to take away that thunder.<br /> <br /> In terms of the cenaculum creation system given in The Inquisition, San Diego is probably a &quot;Strong&quot; cenaculum which will eventually develop into a &quot;Venerable&quot; one. LA's cenaculum is probably &quot;Weak&quot; or &quot;Marginal&quot;. As the older major city, San Francisco probably has an &quot;Average&quot; of stronger cenaculum, and would probably be a better candidate for the location of the provincial (and may have been at one point), but for chronicle purposes and personal taste I'm placing it in San Diego.<br /> <br /> As a &quot;Strong&quot; cenaculum, the location itself has a True Faith rating of 2, each inquisitor gets a stipend of $1500 a month (1995 money), two full time and three part time retainers taking care of it, decent security including a security guard on location at all times, some technology (computers with a LAN, a CD-ROM reader, and even a fax machine!), and two dedicated cars.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;coterie&quot; of hunters (technically a cenacle) based there, I imagine they all have True Faith ratings between 1-5. I might have one have more at 6+. There will be at least one member knowing the Via Necromantiae so they can do exorcisms, and someone perhaps may know one other Theurgy.<br /> <br /> One of the security guards will be one of the condotierri, and as the cenaculum grows and develops, eventually all security guards will be members. They just aren't there yet. The condotierre is the manager of security, and the other guards report to him.<br /> <br /> Besides this cenacle at the San Diego cenaculum itself, there is another one based on John Carpenter's Vampires that are usually on the road elsewhere in the American southwest that report to the San Diego cenaculum. There's a similar cenacle in northern Mexico comprised of Mexican citizens who are officially report to the Central American province, and may even have some weak cenaculum (maybe in Hermosillo, Sonora). However, they coordinate a lot with San Diego especially when they're active in northern Baja California.<br /> <br /> I'll keep the cenacle in LA itself fairly small, maybe only 1-2 members. They mostly collect information, investigate, and attempt to help victims find safety rather than truly &quot;hunt&quot; themselves. They act as local guides to the more experienced cenacles when they show up to do the actual hunting. There's no real reason to keep this cenacle so small except I don't want to take attention away from Reverend Cutler and the other hunter groups we've talked about here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T15:09:20-07:00","id":1552597,"title":"","content":"You would think, given southern California's Spanish mission settlements, that one of the cities or towns there would be one of the oldest Inquisition bases in the US. \ud83e\udd14 <br /> <br /> I often like to think of the Society of Leopold as having a fair amount of associate members. People who are Catholic believers who recognize the existence of supernatural evil and do what they can but aren't &quot;full&quot; members of the Society (and especially not of any of the special subfactions). The police detective who was trained by Jesuits at Catholic school, the Latino street criminal trying to go straight after encountering a demon, the housekeeper spying on her ghoul employeror the like. They aren't Inquisitors but may be put in touch with any who come to town (and may be being scouted for future recruitment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T17:22:05-07:00","id":1552600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552597#post1552597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would think, given southern California's Spanish mission settlements, that one of the cities or towns there would be one of the oldest Inquisition bases in the US. \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only were the Spanish missions founded fairly late in the history of New Spain, large cities in California aren't found until fairly late in the 19th century (even San Francisco didn't start until the Gold Rush). There's just not going to be a lot of vampires there, nor any way to support hunters out there logistically. Plus I'm not sure how Catholic (American) southern California was before mass immigration from Mexico in the second half of the Twentieth Century.<br /> <br /> So I'm happy with what I came up with, but other STs can do what works best for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552597#post1552597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often like to think of the Society of Leopold as having a fair amount of associate members. People who are Catholic believers who recognize the existence of supernatural evil and do what they can but aren't &quot;full&quot; members of the Society (and especially not of any of the special subfactions). The police detective who was trained by Jesuits at Catholic school, the Latino street criminal trying to go straight after encountering a demon, the housekeeper spying on her ghoul employeror the like. They aren't Inquisitors but may be put in touch with any who come to town (and may be being scouted for future recruitment).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are probably correct. This is where the Allies, Contacts, and Retainers are for NPCs who are actually part of the Society of St Leopold. The Society itself includes both clergy, religious brothers and sisters, and the laity. So there's a great deal of variety found among &quot;inquisitors&quot;. Combined with &quot;associates&quot; its network can be pretty far. The one factor that really inhibits membership is how many people actually want to make it their vocation to hunt these supernatural creatures? That has to be exhausting on all levels - mentally, emotionally, physically, spiritually. I imagine there must be a lot of combat veterans who have already faced the horror of war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0oj79zQnf-I\" data-code=\"0oj79zQnf-I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0oj79zQnf-I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Smart, experienced hunters are going to stack as much advantage as they can and minimize their own casualties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T18:10:09-07:00","id":1552601,"title":"","content":"San Diego and Monterey were both founded in the 1770s, with the San Diego mission apparently having about 1400 native converts (exactly how authenticity converted they were is anyone's guess) plus soldiers at the presidio and additional Spanish colonists. If any member(s) of the Society of Leopold did show up there (probably sent from Mexico City), I presume they'd be primarily going up against werewolves (and probably dying unless it was a single lost cub or crazed ronin from one of the Three Brothers), ghosts, or native &quot;witchcraft&quot;.<br /> <br /> And one of the great parts of the Vampire$ novel is how much detail it goes into about the mindset and psychological stress of the kind of people who would hunt monsters for a living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T18:32:46-07:00","id":1552602,"title":"","content":"Regarding Cutler, the Blood, and The Crypt's Sons, in the real world early 90s LA, the Crips outnumbered the Bloods by about three to one. So Cutler has his work cut out for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T20:13:29-07:00","id":1552603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552602#post1552602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Cutler, the Blood, and The Crypt's Sons, in the real world early 90s LA, the Crips outnumbered the Bloods by about three to one. So Cutler has his work cut out for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of this. That's good information to know. I think a similar dynamic would work well for the chronicle. A gang being heavily supported by a powerful vampire anarch gang/barony will have a huge advantage over a gang that simply has a group of hunters at its core. The &quot;victory&quot; for Cutler isn't that the Blood is as big as the Crypts (I imagine he is bothered by having to use a criminal gang at all, but those are the compromises one must make at times), but that the Blood somehow manages to retain its independence (unlike other gangs who are brought to their heel), and that Blood territory is mostly vampire free (hopefully).<br /> <br /> I imagine in fictional LA that the Blood is known for being an especially cruel criminal gang. They probably stake and decapitate various Crypt vampires during the day, and since so many Crypt vampires are very young fledglings and neonates, their bodies don't turn to dust when the vampires day. It just becomes evidence of a murder scene if not secretly disposed of. The police probably consider decapitation some kind of &quot;calling sign&quot; or &quot;gang initiation&quot; of the Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-25T14:45:11-07:00","id":1552649,"title":"","content":"I'm not thinking of any more hunter topics so I am moving on to Wraith. (Like always if someone wants to comment on any previous post, please do so).<br /> <br /> I don't think we're given anything on the Shadowlands of LA. The only thing I am aware of is a very high level one page description of LA in the Wraith 20th Anniversary corebook. In terms of Vampire, I think any of the normal wraith politics or Shadowlands squabbles are unimportant. Only if you are running a very Necromancy heavy chronicle will any of that be important. Instead, I will be taking my usual advice I give others when they ask about incorporating Wraith into Vampire or Werewolf or other game: think about your typical ghost stories and run plots like that instead.<br /> <br /> So what kind of ghost stories might be told in the Free States? Thankfully there are a lot of real world hauntings in LA we can use as inspiration IF any of the PCs are interested in that. We have several well known &quot;haunts&quot; that involve ghosts or other spooky paranormal activities. There are:<br /> <br /> The <b>Cecil Hotel</b> in downtown LA. Various murders, suicides, and disappearances with various people reporting ghosts, unusual sounds, and creepy feelings.<br /> <br /> The Hollywood <b>Roosevelt Hotel</b>. Many celebrities have stayed here, and people have reported seeing the ghosts of Marilyn Monroe, Montgomery Cliff, and I think a few others.<br /> <br /> The <b>Wonderland Murder House</b> in Lauren Canyon. This residence was the scene of a spectacular unsolved crime in 1981 that involves drug dealing, organized crime, and the porn star John Holmes. Ever since people have reported strange activities, possibly from the ghosts of the victims. Since this is so specific, I would use a fictionalized version.<br /> <br /> The &quot;<b>Entity House</b>&quot; of Doris Bither. This woman claimed to have been violenlty attacked and violated by paranormal entities. The story was told in fictionalized versions as the 1978 book The Entity by Frank De Felitta which was turned into a 1982 movie of the same name. Very disturbing. Once again since this is so specific, I would use a fictionalized version of it only.<br /> <br /> The <b>Linda Vista Hospital</b> in Boyle Heights. This was once a railroad association hospital which was converted into a public hospital in the 1970s as use by the railroad association declined. By this time the hospital was quite old and the neighborhood was in decline. In trying to reduce the expenses of running the hospital, its quality declined even as gang related violence saw an increase in treating patients. The hospital gained a bad reputation and was eventually shut down in 1991. Ever since it is claimed to be haunted by a lot of ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Griffith Observatory</b>. People say they have seen James Dean's ghost there.<br /> <br /> The <b>Hollywood Sign</b>. It's supposed to be a frequent suicide spot as people jump to their deaths from the top of its letters.<br /> <br /> The <b>RMS Queen Mary</b> docked at Long Beach. This former luxury ocean liner and WWII troop ship is reported to have many ghosts. It currently serves as a floating restaurant, hotel, and museum. It will temporarily close in late 1992 and reopen in early 1993 due to a change in operators.<br /> <br /> There are, of course, many more places around LA that people claim are haunted, but these tend to be the places that always make people's lists. I don't intend to run any active ghost haunting plots, but if any PCs are interested in exploring this aspect of the World of Darkness, this is where I will direct them first with a combination of celebrity and common ghosts. From there, I'll just have to brainstorm some things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T21:44:53-07:00","id":1552684,"title":"","content":"You could borrow a bit from the movie Tales from the Hood, with a victim of corrupt cops seeking vengeance for their own murder. Maybe tie it in with the LAPD Rampart scandal.<br /> <br /> I'll also mention Clive Barker's novel Coldheart Canyon. <br /> <br /> One wonders what vampires do when their haven is haunted. \ud83e\udd14 I mean, you don't really want to ask favors of the local Giovanni, so do you ever end up with individuals or coteries who specialize in that kind of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T11:20:06-07:00","id":1552703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552684#post1552684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could borrow a bit from the movie Tales from the Hood, with a victim of corrupt cops seeking vengeance for their own murder. Maybe tie it in with the LAPD Rampart scandal.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's obviously lots of ghost stories you can tell in LA. But none of those require the involvement of vampires. It's really a question of whether any of the PCs are interested in investigating or being involved in stories like that, and what kind of stories fit the scene their characters are involved in. There would be different kind of ghost stories depending if the PCs were involved mostly in the LA celebrity circles, gangland street culture, settled in an ethnic community, aiming to build a business/finance empire, etc.<br /> <br /> A fictional version of CRASH will appear in the game, although like all things it depends on whether the PCs get involved. If they are going full Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas, they'll encounter those kind of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552684#post1552684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also mention Clive Barker's novel Coldheart Canyon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not read that book. I have read Barker's Books of Blood, the novella Hellbound Heart, and the Books of the Art series, but not his other stuff. Barker is almost invariably good as long as you like (or tolerate) his idiosyncrasies so I'm sure it's quite good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552684#post1552684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wonders what vampires do when their haven is haunted. \ud83e\udd14 I mean, you don't really want to ask favors of the local Giovanni, so do you ever end up with individuals or coteries who specialize in that kind of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the players want to explore that, the response of the PCs would almost always be, &quot;I move out and find a new haven&quot; - which is not that hard to do in a large city where almost all chronicles are set. Only if the PCs are somehow intimately connected with the haven or the ghosts somehow would they ever both staying, and that requires some discussion between the ST and PCs beforehand either as part of the chronicle pitch, or as part of one or more PCs backstory.<br /> <br /> In terms of how vampires deal with bothersome ghosts in general, it's important to remember you don't need the Necromancy Discipline to defend yourself. Ordinary mortals are able to do Warding and Forbiddance. There are people who have Numina or Paths of Sorcery. It's not impossible for vampires to find such mortals and make the appropriate negotiations/manipulations. <br /> <br /> Or to translate some of that into appropriate Blood Magic rituals. They don't need to be as powerful as the fifth level ritual Ward against Spirits (or Warding Circle) so they can be lower level rituals. Nor do they necessarily need to be limited to Tremere, the setting's insistence of blood magic being exclusive to the Tremere died long, long ago (although I would still make such knowledge very rare). Not to mention certain Merits and Flaws (Spirit Mentor, Haunted, possibly others) that are relevant.<br /> <br /> Vampires with Auspex can detect the auras of ghosts or can use Animalism to speak with animals who can detect ghosts. So it's possible for vampires even with fairly &quot;mundane&quot; Disciplines to detect ghosts, communicate with them, and even possibly make friends and allies to counter other ghosts. There's a lot you can do.<br /> <br /> It's just a question whether any Kindred or coterie &quot;specializes&quot; as you say and can become a resource for others. I figure in most large domains there are probably at least one. To your point, in some chronicles there probably should be especially if you are going to include ghosts as a prominent element. In a domain as large as Los Angeles, there probably are multiple such Kindred or coteries. I have some NPC candidates in mind, but won't assign them unless this becomes something the players want or seek.<br /> <br /> I've been in too many LARPs where STs just let Giovanni PCs run roughshod over everyone else because of the idea that unless you have Necromancy, you can't do anything. I always hated that. Necromancy needs to be just as useful as any other Discipline or Path, and the higher levels just as much as others, but it is not some instant win you can't beat. There are things you can do to balance it out even if Necromancy is the most powerful version of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T12:12:05-07:00","id":1552705,"title":"","content":"In the case of the Tales from the Hood story, it would make an interesting idea for one of the Risen, which might force local vampires to take an interest when stories about some sort of unkillable boogieman stalking corrupt cops might spark fears of a possible Masquerade breach. But only if you really wanted PCs to get involved with that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And I suppose if you wanted to amuse players of a certain age, you could have the events of the original Poltergeist film have actually happened and now, ten years later, have become part of local Orange County folklore in a somewhat distorted form in this pre-internet time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T18:09:53-07:00","id":1552820,"title":"","content":"It's been so long since I have looked at any Changeling books, so I can't remember if LA was ever mentioned or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T23:33:32-07:00","id":1552823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements?p=1552820#post1552820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been so long since I have looked at any Changeling books, so I can't remember if LA was ever mentioned or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there's been some mention somewhere. However, I won't be addressing it (others are free to do so though). I have a lot of issues with the Changeling setting and make extensive changes from canon in regards to fey in my WoD games. While I could cobble some things together from actual California folklore and basic faerie tropes to address how the fey are in SoCal, the fact is I very much doubt my players have any interest in that crossover. There's just not any natural crossover between vampire and fairies that my players would be interested in, especially not in the heavily urban environment of LA.<br /> <br /> However, I will likely mention the Dark Watchers at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T10:53:44-07:00","id":1552883,"title":"","content":"Of all the Old World of Darkness lines, Changeling felt like the one that would be happiest doing its thing in another timeline not really connected to whatever was going on elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Heck, making Changeling glamour something that could keep the World of Darkness at bay - though only for a time - is a potentially interesting wrinkle to throw in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}